00:09:59,205 --> 00:10:01,125
Ah, Justine !
Ah, Justine!

177
00:10:01,285 --> 00:10:03,645
Justine ?
Justine?

178
00:10:07,125 --> 00:10:08,605
Médiawan, bonjour.
Médiawan, how can I help you?

179
00:10:09,525 --> 00:10:11,845
Ah, bonjour, Madame de Serisy.
Oh, hello, Mrs. de Serisy.

180
00:10:12,845 --> 00:10:16,165
Oui ! Non, en fait, c'est Noémie. Ravie de faire votre connaissance.
Yes! No, actually, this is Noémie.
Lovely to meet you.

181
00:10:16,645 --> 00:10:17,925
Justine est occupée pour le moment.
Justine is busy right now.

182
00:10:19,245 --> 00:10:22,125
Oui ! Il est sorti déjeuner.
Yes! He's gone out for lunch.

183
00:10:24,965 --> 00:10:27,445
Il a écrit pour dire qu'il était bloqué au bureau ?
He wrote to say
he was stuck at the office?

184
00:10:27,525 --> 00:10:29,285
Alors je crois que c'est--
Then I think it's--

185
00:10:31,605 --> 00:10:34,165
Madame de Serisy ? Oui, c'est Justine.
Mrs. de Serisy? Yes, this is Justine.

186
00:10:34,685 --> 00:10:36,525
Bien sûr qu'il est là, il est en ligne.
Of course he's here, he's taking a call.

187
00:10:36,605 --> 00:10:39,285
Il vous rappelle dès qu'il a raccroché. Bonne journée.
He'll call you back
as soon as he hangs up. Have a good day.

188
00:10:41,845 --> 00:10:43,485
C'est moi et moi seule qui réponds à ce téléphone.
Nobody but me picks up this phone.

189
00:10:43,565 --> 00:10:46,005
Surtout si c'est sa femme. C'est compris ?
Especially if it's his wife. Undertood?

190
00:10:46,085 --> 00:10:47,405
Oui, bien sûr, d'accord.
Yes, of course, sure.

191
00:10:47,965 --> 00:10:49,885
Je suis désolée, je voulais aider--
I'm sorry, I wanted to help--

192
00:10:49,965 --> 00:10:50,805
Vous n'avez pas aidé.
You didn't.

193
00:10:51,365 --> 00:10:52,645
La prochaine fois, abstenez-vous.
Next time, try to hold back.

194
00:10:53,205 --> 00:10:54,365
Oui. Bien sûr.
Yes. Sure.

195
00:11:01,765 --> 00:11:02,925
Oui, Jean-Luc.
Yes, Jean-Luc.

196
00:11:06,205 --> 00:11:07,085
C'est qui ?
Who's that?

197
00:11:07,765 --> 00:11:09,125
Vous ne connaissez pas Elise Formain ?
You don't know Elise Formain?

198
00:11:09,725 --> 00:11:11,485
La plus grande agent de StarMédia.
StarMédia's biggest agent.

199
00:11:11,925 --> 00:11:14,845
Elle nous a soufflé Nathalie Baye et Dany Boon. Et d'autres encore.
She snatched Nathalie Baye
and Dany Boon from us. And others too.

200
00:11:14,925 --> 00:11:16,325
Qu'est-ce qu'elle fait là ?
What is she doing here?

201
00:11:17,085 --> 00:11:19,005
Vous croyez que StarMédia va racheter ASK ?
Do you think StarMédia
is going to buy ASK?

202
00:11:20,085 --> 00:11:20,925
Gabriel !
Gabriel!

203
00:11:29,365 --> 00:11:31,805
Si elle veut des parts, on ne peut pas négocier--
If she wants shares, we can't negotiate--

204
00:11:31,885 --> 00:11:33,565
Qu'est-ce qu'Elise Formain fait ici ?
What is Elise Formain doing here?

205
00:11:33,645 --> 00:11:34,925
La porte, s'il vous plaît.
The door, please.

206
00:11:35,685 --> 00:11:38,125
-Donc-- -Fermez la porte, s'il vous plaît.
-So--
-Shut the door, please.

207
00:11:41,685 --> 00:11:43,805
Qu'est-ce que nos concurrents font ici ?
What are our competitors doing here?

208
00:11:43,885 --> 00:11:46,205
Alors… On attend encore quelqu'un ?
So… Are we expecting anyone else?

209
00:11:50,005 --> 00:11:52,525
Vous vous souvenez des conséquences du départ de Mathias ?
You remember the consequences
of Mathias leaving?

210
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:54,245
C'était avant…
That was before…

211
00:11:54,845 --> 00:11:57,045
Parce qu'aujourd'hui, ce qu'on a, c'est…
Because now, what we have is…

212
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:01,685
Voilà.
There.

213
00:12:02,205 --> 00:12:04,005
Plus Daniel Auteuil. Et bien d'autres.
Plus Daniel Auteuil. And many more.

214
00:12:04,565 --> 00:12:06,125
On ne peut pas laisser StarMédia racheter ASK.
We can't let Starmédia buy ASK.

215
00:12:06,205 --> 00:12:09,285
Personne ne rachète personne. On recrute.
No one is buying anyone. We're hiring.

216
00:12:09,845 --> 00:12:11,485
Elise Formain nous rejoint chez ASK.
Elise Formain is joining us at ASK.

217
00:12:12,245 --> 00:12:13,805
-Avec tous ses clients. -Pardon ?
-With all her clients.
-Excuse me?

218
00:12:14,365 --> 00:12:15,405
C'est une plaisanterie ?
Is this a joke?

219
00:12:16,085 --> 00:12:17,965
-Et pourquoi ? -Vous demandez pourquoi ?
-And why?
-You're asking why?

220
00:12:18,765 --> 00:12:22,085
Le tableau n'est pas assez clair ? Il faut que je vous fasse un dessin ?
Is the table not clear enough?
Do I have to spell it out?

221
00:12:23,165 --> 00:12:26,685
Elle a un portefeuille de clients impressionnant, certes, mais ce n'est pas tout ce qui compte.
She's got an impressive list of clients,
sure, but that's not all that counts.

222
00:12:28,245 --> 00:12:30,685
Cette nana, c'est Mathias en talons hauts.
This chick, it's Mathias with high heels.

223
00:12:30,765 --> 00:12:32,485
C'est Le Diable s'habille en Prada--
It's The Devil Wears Prada--

224
00:12:32,565 --> 00:12:34,805
On a compris l'idée. Même moi je vois les références.
We get the gist.
Even I get the references.

225
00:12:34,885 --> 00:12:36,725
N'en faisons pas tout un fromage.
Let's not blow this out of proportion.

226
00:12:36,805 --> 00:12:40,645
Allez. Je ne suis pas sa plus grande fan, mais ce n'est pas un monstre non plus.
Come on. I'm not her biggest fan,
but she's not a monster either.

227
00:12:40,725 --> 00:12:41,565
Gabriel a raison.
Gabriel is right.

228
00:12:42,605 --> 00:12:43,685
Et si on votait ?
Why don't we vote?

229
00:12:43,765 --> 00:12:45,085
-Quoi ? -Merci, Hicham.
-What?
-Thanks, Hicham.

230
00:12:45,165 --> 00:12:46,525
Mais il n'y a pas de filet de sécurité.
But there's no security net.

231
00:12:46,605 --> 00:12:48,285
Qu'est-ce que vous voulez dire, « pas de filet de sécurité » ?
What do you mean, "no security net"?

232
00:12:48,365 --> 00:12:50,845
Je n'ai plus aucune liquidité disponible.
I don't have any money left at the ready.

233
00:12:52,125 --> 00:12:54,805
Donc si vous ne rééquilibrez pas les comptes par vous-mêmes, c'est terminé.
So if you can't redress
the balance yourselves, it's over.

234
00:12:55,645 --> 00:12:56,485
On y va.
Let's do it.

235
00:12:56,565 --> 00:12:59,125
Qui est pour ne pas recruter Elise Formain ?
Who is in favor
of not hiring Elise Formain?

236
00:13:00,085 --> 00:13:02,805
Sachant que c'est la fin si on ne trouve pas une autre solution.
Knowing that it's curtains
if we don't find another solution.

237
00:13:03,885 --> 00:13:07,005
Qui est pour recruter Elise, sachant qu'on récupère tous ses clients ?
Who is in favor of hiring Elise,
knowing we'll get all her clients?

238
00:13:07,085 --> 00:13:10,765
Ce qui nous permettrait de payer le loyer, les salaires, et de renvoyer la compta à son étage ?
Allowing us to pay rent, our salaries,
and send accounting back to their floor?

239
00:13:11,805 --> 00:13:13,925
-Non… -Désolé.
-No…
-Sorry.

240
00:13:23,525 --> 00:13:25,445
Je ne peux pas travailler dans ces conditions !
I can't work like this!

241
00:13:25,525 --> 00:13:27,485
Il y a un problème avec la photocopieuse ?
Is there a problem with the copy machine?

242
00:13:27,565 --> 00:13:29,405
Non, c'est la chose la plus sympa ici.
No, it's the most friendly thing here.

243
00:13:29,965 --> 00:13:33,485
Tu n'as pas remarqué que personne ne nous parle ?
You haven't noticed
that no one talks to us?

244
00:13:34,645 --> 00:13:35,925
Non, je n'avais pas remarqué.
No, I hadn't noticed.

245
00:13:40,925 --> 00:13:44,205
Mathias. Ma corbeille à papier n'est jamais vidée.
Mathias. My waste paper basket
never gets emptied.

246
00:13:45,165 --> 00:13:46,845
Elle se remplit même pendant la nuit.
It even fills up overnight.

247
00:13:47,765 --> 00:13:49,125
Je ne comprends pas.
I don't follow.

248
00:13:51,405 --> 00:13:53,725
Je crois que Justine
I think that Justine

249
00:13:54,205 --> 00:13:56,805
a arrangé ça avec le personnel de ménage.
fixed it with the cleaning staff.

250
00:13:56,885 --> 00:13:57,885
Pour me persécuter.
To persecute me.

251
00:13:57,965 --> 00:14:00,805
Non, non… Écoute, calme-toi.
No, no… Look, calm down.

252
00:14:00,885 --> 00:14:04,765
On vient d'arriver. C'est tout à fait normal. Il faut trouver nos marques. S'installer.
We just got here. It's all very normal.
We have to find our bearings. Settle in.

253
00:14:04,845 --> 00:14:06,725
ASK, c'était une famille, un cocon.
ASK was a family, a cocoon.

254
00:14:06,805 --> 00:14:08,485
Ici, c'est très différent. C'est peut-être
It's very different here. It may be

255
00:14:08,565 --> 00:14:10,805
pour le mieux. Là-bas, tout était mélangé.
for the best. Back there,
everything was mixed-up.

256
00:14:10,885 --> 00:14:13,285
Plus de frontières entre vie professionnelle et vie personnelle.
No boundaries
between professional and personal lives.

257
00:14:13,365 --> 00:14:15,685
Tu n'es vraiment pas en position de te plaindre.
You're not really
in any position to complain.

258
00:14:16,685 --> 00:14:17,965
Je suis désolé, Mathias,
I'm sorry, Mathias,

259
00:14:18,045 --> 00:14:20,965
mais j'ai besoin de convivialité dans ma vie !
but I need conviviality in my life!

260
00:14:21,045 --> 00:14:22,925
Je suis isolé au travail, on ne se voit pas.
I'm isolated at work, we don't socialize.

261
00:14:23,005 --> 00:14:25,045
On pourrait au moins inviter des gens à dîner !
We could at least have people over
for dinner!

262
00:14:25,525 --> 00:14:26,685
Qui, par exemple ?
Like whom?

263
00:14:26,765 --> 00:14:27,965
Des amis.
Like friends.

264
00:14:28,045 --> 00:14:31,405
Tu organisais des dîners avec Catherine, je le sais, c'est moi qui faisais les invitations.
You had dinner parties with Catherine,
I know, I was doing the invites.

265
00:14:32,365 --> 00:14:35,285
Alors… il me semble que tu ne veux pas me présenter.
So… it seems to me
you don't want to introduce me.

266
00:14:36,685 --> 00:14:38,005
Tu as honte de moi ?
Are you ashamed of me?

267
00:14:38,485 --> 00:14:39,925
Je ne vois plus mes amis.
I don't see my friends anymore.

268
00:14:41,285 --> 00:14:43,405
Je n'ai jamais su entretenir une vie sociale.
I was never good
at maintaining a social life.

269
00:14:44,325 --> 00:14:47,965
Catherine s'en occupait, et après tout, c'étaient ses amis.
Catherine handled it,
and after all, they were her friends.

270
00:14:48,605 --> 00:14:49,485
Oh, je suis désolé.
Oh, I'm sorry.

271
00:14:50,805 --> 00:14:53,245
Pardon, excuse-moi, je ne savais pas.
I'm sorry, forgive me, I didn't know.

272
00:14:57,405 --> 00:14:59,765
Ne t'inquiète pas, on ne va pas se laisser faire.
Don't worry, we're not going to give in.

273
00:14:59,845 --> 00:15:02,605
Pas question de vivre comme des rats crevés. D'accord ?
No way are we going to live
like dead rats. OK?

274
00:15:05,965 --> 00:15:07,245
Je suis content de t'avoir parlé.
I'm glad I talked to you.

275
00:15:10,285 --> 00:15:11,485
-Tiens. -Merci.
-Here.
-Thanks.

276
00:15:11,565 --> 00:15:12,485
De rien.
You're welcome.

277
00:15:14,165 --> 00:15:16,405
Tout le monde, s'il vous plaît !
Everyone, please!

278
00:15:16,485 --> 00:15:18,565
Élise, la parole est à toi.
Elise, the floor is yours.

279
00:15:19,925 --> 00:15:23,445
Eh bien, merci à tous de m'accueillir chez ASK.
Well, thank you all
for welcoming me to ASK.

280
00:15:23,525 --> 00:15:24,485
Soyons honnêtes,
Let's be honest,

281
00:15:24,565 --> 00:15:27,765
j'ai une certaine mauvaise réputation chez les concurrents.
I have something
of a bad reputation among competitors.

282
00:15:28,245 --> 00:15:29,565
Et pour être franche,
And to be honest,

283
00:15:30,205 --> 00:15:32,005
je la mérite peut-être, dans un sens.
I may, in a sense, deserve it.

284
00:15:32,965 --> 00:15:35,165
Mais tout est une question de point de vue.
But it's all a matter of perspective.

285
00:15:35,885 --> 00:15:39,045
Alors, après 20 ans chez Starmédia,
So, after 20 years at Starmédia,

286
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:41,005
c'est un nouveau départ pour moi.
this is a new start for me.

287
00:15:41,085 --> 00:15:42,565
Je n'arrive pas seule.
I'm not coming in alone.

288
00:15:42,645 --> 00:15:45,965
Je vous présente Marine et Océane, mes deux merveilleuses assistantes.
Let me introduce Marine and Océane,
my two wonderful assistants.

289
00:15:46,045 --> 00:15:47,205
Bonjour.
Hello.

290
00:15:47,805 --> 00:15:51,765
J'ai entendu dire qu'elle a eu 3 maris, 1 enfant avec chacun et 200 amants. C'est une ogresse.
I've heard she's had 3 husbands, 1 child
with each and 200 lovers. She's an ogress.

291
00:15:51,845 --> 00:15:53,285
…notamment Hervé et Camille.
…especially Hervé and Camille.

292
00:15:53,965 --> 00:15:56,565
J'ai entendu beaucoup de bien sur les juniors d'ASK.
I've heard a lot of good things
about ASK's juniors.

293
00:15:56,645 --> 00:15:59,045
Vous êtes audacieux, intuitifs.
You're bold, intuitive.

294
00:15:59,725 --> 00:16:02,165
Deux qualités qui font d'excellents agents.
Two qualities that make excellent agents.

295
00:16:02,245 --> 00:16:04,045
On dit du bien de nous ?
People are saying good things about us?

296
00:16:04,125 --> 00:16:06,525
Oubliez « ogresse ». « Connaisseuse » est plus approprié.
Forget "ogress." "Connoisseur"
is more appropriate.

297
00:16:06,605 --> 00:16:09,765
Andréa, je sais que ce n'est pas facile pour toi.
Andréa, I know it's not easy for you.

298
00:16:09,845 --> 00:16:11,645
On ne s'est jamais vraiment entendues.
We've never really got along.

299
00:16:11,725 --> 00:16:14,765
Et pourtant, j'ai toujours admiré ton travail.
And yet, I've always admired your work.

300
00:16:15,405 --> 00:16:17,525
Tu as beaucoup donné à cette agence.
You've put a lot into this agency.

301
00:16:18,085 --> 00:16:20,725
Tu es un vrai battant. Comme moi.
You're a true fighter. Like me.

302
00:16:21,565 --> 00:16:23,725
Je suis sûr qu'on a beaucoup à apprendre l'un de l'autre.
I'm sure we have a lot to learn
from each other.

303
00:16:24,205 --> 00:16:25,285
Merci de me faire confiance.
Thanks for trusting me.

304
00:16:25,965 --> 00:16:26,965
Merci.
Thank you.

305
00:16:28,565 --> 00:16:31,045
Arlette. Chère Arlette.
Arlette. Dearest Arlette.

306
00:16:32,205 --> 00:16:34,485
-On s'est souvent accrochés. -C'est le moins qu'on puisse dire.
-We've had our fair share of run-ins.
-I'll say.

307
00:16:36,165 --> 00:16:37,405
Désolé pour Jean Rochefort.
Sorry about Jean Rochefort.

308
00:16:38,005 --> 00:16:40,885
Et moi pour Piccoli. Quitte à quitte.
And I'm sorry about Piccoli. Even-steven.

309
00:16:42,605 --> 00:16:43,845
Quant à toi, Gabriel--
As for you, Gabriel--

310
00:16:43,925 --> 00:16:47,125
Désolé, je n'ai pas le temps pour ça. J'ai du travail.
Sorry, I don't have time for this.
I have work to do.

311
00:16:49,405 --> 00:16:52,765
Oh, oui. Oui, je voudrais porter un toast. Écoutez bien.
Oh, yes. Yes, I would like
to propose a toast. Listen up.

312
00:16:54,405 --> 00:16:57,885
À la mort de nos principes ! Samuel Kerr, si vous regardez…
To the death of our principles!
Samuel Kerr, if you're watching…

313
00:16:58,525 --> 00:17:01,045
Eh bien, détournez les yeux. Pour votre bien.
Well, look away. For your own good.

314
00:17:08,365 --> 00:17:09,364
En tout cas…
In any case…

315
00:17:11,205 --> 00:17:13,245
tu ne m'as jamais fait de mal, et tu travailles dur.
you never did me any wrong,
and you work hard.

316
00:17:13,324 --> 00:17:15,604
Avant de partir pour Londres, je voulais
Before leaving for London, I wanted

317
00:17:16,165 --> 00:17:17,245
accueillir Élise.
to welcome Elise.

318
00:17:19,604 --> 00:17:20,604
À Élise !
To Elise!

319
00:17:21,324 --> 00:17:23,005
À Élise !
To Elise!

320
00:17:23,485 --> 00:17:25,084
Merci.
Thank you.

321
00:17:25,765 --> 00:17:26,965
Merci.
Thank you.

322
00:17:31,445 --> 00:17:32,285
Merde.
Shit.

323
00:17:34,405 --> 00:17:37,565
Qui s'en fout de qui vous êtes en dehors de cette cuisine ?
Who cares who you are
outside of this kitchen ?

324
00:17:37,645 --> 00:17:40,485
Dès que vous enfilez votre veste et votre tablier, vous devenez un tout.
Once you put on your jacket
and your apron, you become a whole.

325
00:17:40,565 --> 00:17:41,805
Et un tout, c'est une brigade.
And a whole is a brigade.

326
00:17:41,885 --> 00:17:43,765
Et une brigade, c'est une famille. Et maintenant…
And a brigade is a family. And now…

327
00:17:43,845 --> 00:17:46,005
Maintenant, j'ai besoin de ma famille.
Now, I need my family.

328
00:17:46,085 --> 00:17:48,645
Parce que ce restaurant, c'est ma vie. OK ?
Because this restaurant is my life. OK?

329
00:17:49,125 --> 00:17:53,205
Alors si on ne peut pas surprendre les gens, si on ne peut pas les rendre heureux…
So if we can't surprise people,
if we can't make them happy…

330
00:17:53,845 --> 00:17:56,445
C'est fini. Donc quand vous mettez votre toge--
Then, it's over.
So when you put your toga--

331
00:17:56,525 --> 00:17:58,005
La toque.
The toque.

332
00:17:58,085 --> 00:17:59,645
Pardon. Quand vous mettez votre toque…
Sorry. When you put on your toque…

333
00:17:59,725 --> 00:18:01,685
Quand vous attachez votre brigade…
When you fasten your brigade…

334
00:18:01,765 --> 00:18:02,965
-Votre tablier. -Vous devenez…
-Your apron.
-You become…

335
00:18:03,045 --> 00:18:03,925
-Quoi ? -Votre tablier.
-What?
-Your apron.

336
00:18:04,005 --> 00:18:04,845
Votre tablier !
Your apron!

337
00:18:05,445 --> 00:18:06,725
C'est mon restaurant, bon sang !
It's my restaurant, damn it!

338
00:18:06,805 --> 00:18:07,925
Et… et…
And… and…

339
00:18:08,445 --> 00:18:09,765
Et je veux dire, allez-y !
And I mean, go for it!

340
00:18:10,245 --> 00:18:11,125
Allez-y !
Go for it!

341
00:18:11,205 --> 00:18:12,045
Donc…
So…

342
00:18:13,045 --> 00:18:14,325
Essayez de…
Try to…

343
00:18:14,405 --> 00:18:16,445
Vous savez. C'est ma vie… Et la vie…
You know. It's my life… And life…

344
00:18:17,165 --> 00:18:18,085
OK. Coupez !
OK. Cut!

345
00:18:18,165 --> 00:18:19,405
On coupe.
We're cut.

346
00:18:19,485 --> 00:18:20,565
Merde.
Shit.

347
00:18:22,765 --> 00:18:24,565
Bon… Bon, je vois.
Right… Right, I see.

348
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:27,085
Oui. C'est la 12e prise qu'il rate.
Yes. It's the 12th take he's screwed up.

349
00:18:27,165 --> 00:18:29,645
Il perd la voix, il oublie son texte.
He loses his voice, forgets his lines.

350
00:18:31,445 --> 00:18:34,125
-On recommence ! -Ouais.
-Let's try it again!
-Yeah.

351
00:18:34,205 --> 00:18:35,565
-José. -Ouais.
-José.
-Yeah.

352
00:18:35,645 --> 00:18:37,965
-Tu dois leur crier dessus. -Oui, oui.
-You have to yell at them.
-Yes, yes.

353
00:18:38,045 --> 00:18:40,285
N'hésite pas. Vraiment, vas-y franchement.
Don't hesitate. Really rip into them.

354
00:18:40,365 --> 00:18:41,765
-Oui. Je sais. Oui. -OK ?
-Yes. I know. Yes.
-OK?

355
00:18:41,845 --> 00:18:43,765
Oh, et la caméra…
Oh, and the camera…

356
00:18:44,885 --> 00:18:45,925
Ne la regarde pas.
Don't look at it.

357
00:18:46,005 --> 00:18:47,205
Je la regardais ?
Was I looking at it?

358
00:18:47,285 --> 00:18:49,285
-Un peu. Ouais. -Oh. Désolé.
-A little. Yeah.
-Oh. Sorry.

359
00:18:51,605 --> 00:18:53,005
On recommence.
Let's try it again.

360
00:18:53,685 --> 00:18:55,445
Moteur. Clap.
Rolling. Clapperboard.

361
00:18:57,565 --> 00:18:58,565
Action !
Action!

362
00:18:59,285 --> 00:19:03,365
La vérité, c'est que je m'en fous de qui tu es en dehors de cette cuisine. D'accord ?
Truth is, I don't care who you are
outside of this kitchen. All right?

363
00:19:03,445 --> 00:19:04,765
Quand tu enfiles ta veste…
When you put on your jacket…

364
00:19:04,845 --> 00:19:06,445
Dès que tu… que tu…
As soon as you… as you…

365
00:19:06,525 --> 00:19:08,365
Tu attaches ton tablier…
You fasten your apron…

366
00:19:08,445 --> 00:19:10,085
Voilà… Tu dois être…
Right… You have to be…

367
00:19:10,165 --> 00:19:11,925
Conscient… merde.
Aware… damn it.

368
00:19:12,005 --> 00:19:13,405
Ça recommence, merde.
It's back, damn it.

369
00:19:13,485 --> 00:19:15,325
-On s'en fout. -Je suis désolé.
-Fuck it.
-I'm sorry.

370
00:19:16,045 --> 00:19:17,845
-Coupez, on fait une pause. -Zut…
-Cut, let's take five.
-Darn…

371
00:19:19,325 --> 00:19:21,125
Un verre d'eau avec…
A glass of water with…

372
00:19:21,205 --> 00:19:22,525
une paille, s'il vous plaît ? Parce que…
a straw please? Because…

373
00:19:23,085 --> 00:19:25,045
-Ça recommence. -Qu'est-ce que je fais maintenant ?
-It's back.
-What do I do now?

374
00:19:25,125 --> 00:19:26,165
J'appelle un sorcier ?
Call a witch doctor?

375
00:19:27,165 --> 00:19:28,645
Non, c'est moi le sorcier.
No, I'm the witch doctor.

376
00:19:33,765 --> 00:19:34,605
Laurence ?
Laurence?

377
00:19:35,165 --> 00:19:37,285
Bonjour. Vous avez une minute ?
Hi. Do you have a minute?

378
00:19:37,365 --> 00:19:39,485
Je suis Andréa Martel, l'agent de José.
I'm Andréa Martel, José's agent.

379
00:19:40,365 --> 00:19:42,725
Il va bien ? Parce qu'on est en difficulté ici.
Is he OK? Because we're struggling here.

380
00:19:44,045 --> 00:19:45,125
Je m'en excuse à l'avance,
I apologize in advance,

381
00:19:45,205 --> 00:19:48,805
je vais essayer d'y aller doucement mais ce n'est pas vraiment mon domaine.
I'll try to tread carefully
but it's not really in my department.

382
00:19:50,605 --> 00:19:52,565
José m'a parlé de votre liaison il y a 20 ans.
José told me about your affair
20 years ago.

383
00:19:53,805 --> 00:19:54,765
Voilà.
Right.

384
00:19:54,845 --> 00:19:59,125
Et Laurence, vraiment, j'imagine la douleur, les…
And Laurence, really,
I can imagine the pain, the…

385
00:19:59,765 --> 00:20:01,445
Les questions sans réponse.
The unanswered questions.

386
00:20:02,245 --> 00:20:06,165
Il se comporte comme ça parce qu'il se sent coupable de ne pas s'être présenté.
He's acting like this because
he feels guilty about not showing up.

387
00:20:06,245 --> 00:20:09,765
À l'hôtel, il y a 20 ans. Et ça lui ferait du bien
To the hotel, 20 years ago.
And it'd make him feel better

388
00:20:09,845 --> 00:20:11,845
de savoir que vous ne lui en voulez pas.
to know that you don't hold any grudges.

389
00:20:11,925 --> 00:20:14,165
Je veux dire que vous avez tourné la page, je suppose.
I mean that you're healed, I guess.

390
00:20:14,245 --> 00:20:15,925
Si c'est le cas, bien sûr.
If you are healed, that is.

391
00:20:17,125 --> 00:20:18,245
Quel soulagement.
Wow, what a relief.

392
00:20:19,045 --> 00:20:21,445
Je me suis sentie horrible depuis le début du tournage.
I've felt awful since the beginning
of the shoot.

393
00:20:22,365 --> 00:20:23,605
Je croyais qu'il m'en voulait.
I thought he was mad at me.

394
00:20:24,565 --> 00:20:26,645
Moi non plus, je ne suis pas allée à l'hôtel, il y a 20 ans.
I didn't go to the hotel either,
20 years ago.

395
00:20:30,405 --> 00:20:34,405
Ce que José et moi avons vécu était intense. Ça comptait beaucoup.
What José and I had was intense.
It meant a lot.

396
00:20:34,485 --> 00:20:37,005
Mais ce n'était pas fait pour durer. Et c'était il y a longtemps.
But it wasn't meant to last.
And it was a long time ago.

397
00:20:39,005 --> 00:20:40,445
Vous vous êtes posé un lapin mutuellement.
You stood each other up.

398
00:20:41,125 --> 00:20:42,765
On peut dire ça comme ça.
I guess you can say that.

399
00:20:44,245 --> 00:20:45,925
Une comédie romantique à l'envers.
A reverse romantic comedy.

400
00:20:47,005 --> 00:20:48,125
Laurence.
Laurence.

401
00:20:48,205 --> 00:20:49,365
Quand vous voulez.
Whenever you want.

402
00:20:50,445 --> 00:20:52,205
-Je dois y aller. -Pas de problème.
-I have to go.
-No problem.

403
00:20:52,765 --> 00:20:54,685
Alors c'est bon ? Parfait.
Then we're good? Excellent.

404
00:20:54,765 --> 00:20:56,925
Tout le monde en position, s'il vous plaît !
Everyone get into position, please!

405
00:20:58,085 --> 00:20:59,205
Gabriel ?
Gabriel?

406
00:20:59,285 --> 00:21:00,605
-Élise. -Pas maintenant !
-Elise.
-Not now!

407
00:21:00,685 --> 00:21:02,885
Attends ! Attends, attends, attends !
Wait! Wait, wait, wait!

408
00:21:02,965 --> 00:21:04,165
Fermeture des portes.
Doors closing.

409
00:21:04,245 --> 00:21:05,605
Pardon, je ne vous avais pas vu.
Sorry, I didn't see you there.

410
00:21:06,165 --> 00:21:07,005
Ouais…
Yeah…

411
00:21:09,045 --> 00:21:11,525
Tu ne crois pas qu'on devrait se parler, tous les deux ?
Don't you think the two of us should talk?

412
00:21:11,605 --> 00:21:14,645
Je comprends que mon arrivée te reste en travers de la gorge.
I understand
that my arrival sticks in your craw.

413
00:21:15,965 --> 00:21:17,525
Désolé. SMS.
Sorry. Text message.

414
00:21:23,645 --> 00:21:26,205
-Qu'est-ce que tu fais ? -Je crée les conditions du dialogue.
-What are you doing?
-Creating the conditions for dialog.

415
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:29,285
On doit parler, pour clarifier l'atmosphère.
We need to talk, to clear the atmosphere.

416
00:21:29,365 --> 00:21:31,525
L'atmosphère est très claire. Tout va bien.
The atmosphere is very clear.
Everything's fine.

417
00:21:33,805 --> 00:21:36,965
Hé ! On ne peut pas retenir les gens contre leur gré,
Hey!
You can't hold people against their will,

418
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:38,245
c'est une séquestration !
it's sequestration!

419
00:21:41,325 --> 00:21:44,045
Alors appelle les flics. Au lieu d'envoyer des textos imaginaires.
So, call the cops.
Instead of sending imaginary texts.

420
00:21:44,605 --> 00:21:45,765
Tu te fous de moi ?
Are you kidding me?

421
00:21:54,725 --> 00:21:55,685
Merde, non.
Shit, no.

422
00:21:57,005 --> 00:21:57,845
Oh, non.
Oh, no.

423
00:21:59,205 --> 00:22:01,445
Tu ne pouvais pas m'inviter à prendre un café comme tout le monde ?
Couldn't you invite me out for coffee
like normal?

424
00:22:06,125 --> 00:22:07,125
Ça va ?
You're all right?

425
00:22:07,205 --> 00:22:08,205
Non, je suis…
No, I'm…

426
00:22:08,845 --> 00:22:09,765
claustrophobe.
claustrophobic.

427
00:22:12,565 --> 00:22:14,245
-Merde. -Très claustrophobe.
-Shit.
-Very claustrophobic.

428
00:22:14,925 --> 00:22:15,765
C'est nul.
That sucks.

429
00:22:16,325 --> 00:22:17,165
Allez.
Come on.

430
00:22:18,645 --> 00:22:19,485
Putain.
Fuck.

431
00:22:22,285 --> 00:22:25,885
Allô ? À l'aide, je suis coincée avec Élise Formain !
Hello? Help, I'm stuck with Elise Formain!

432
00:22:32,805 --> 00:22:39,805
DÉJEUNER ?
LUNCH?

433
00:22:43,205 --> 00:22:48,285
COINCÉE AU BOULOT DSL
STUCK AT WORK SRY

434
00:22:48,365 --> 00:22:50,845
DSL, DÉBORDÉE AUSSI
SRY, ALSO SWAMPED

435
00:22:50,925 --> 00:22:54,885
Noémie. J'ai organisé un dîner chez moi demain soir.
Noémie. I set up a dinner party
for tomorrow evening at home.

436
00:22:54,965 --> 00:22:56,445
Super ! Avec qui ?
Oh, great! Who with?

437
00:22:57,005 --> 00:22:58,085
Igor et sa femme.
Igor and his wife.

438
00:23:01,605 --> 00:23:02,565
Génial.
Terrific.

439
00:23:04,325 --> 00:23:05,285
Oui, José ?
Yeah, José?

440
00:23:05,365 --> 00:23:08,525
T'as eu mon message ? Désolé, j'ai dû filer au bureau.
Did you get my message?
Sorry, I had to run back to the office.

441
00:23:08,605 --> 00:23:11,205
Tu vois ? Laurence n'est pas venue à ton rendez-vous non plus.
See? Laurence didn't turn up
for your date either.

442
00:23:11,285 --> 00:23:13,965
Oui, donc tu peux arrêter de culpabiliser et…
Yes, so now you can stop feeling guilty
and…

443
00:23:14,445 --> 00:23:15,845
Te concentrer sur ton travail.
Focus on your work.

444
00:23:16,885 --> 00:23:18,485
Ouais, Laurence est super.
Yeah, Laurence is great.

445
00:23:19,285 --> 00:23:21,765
Vous devriez vous parler, ça va arranger les choses.
The 2 of you should talk,
it'll smooth everything out.

446
00:23:23,045 --> 00:23:24,565
OK. Bon.
OK. Well.

447
00:23:24,645 --> 00:23:26,565
Profite bien du tournage, Jojo. Salut.
Enjoy the shoot, Jojo. Bye.

448
00:23:29,325 --> 00:23:31,285
Ça va prendre combien de temps ?
How long is this going to take?

449
00:23:31,365 --> 00:23:33,125
On a beaucoup de clients qui passent par ici.
Many clients come through here.

450
00:23:33,205 --> 00:23:35,525
Ils prendront les escaliers comme tout le monde.
They'll have to take the stairs
like everyone else.

451
00:23:35,605 --> 00:23:38,005
Pour les acteurs, monter des marches, ça se passe à Cannes,
For actors, walking up the stairs
happens in Cannes,

452
00:23:38,085 --> 00:23:39,245
et à Cannes seulement.
and Cannes only.

453
00:23:40,645 --> 00:23:41,965
Vous voulez un tapis rouge ?
Do you want a red carpet?

454
00:23:55,085 --> 00:23:56,325
Vous pouvez m'aider ?
Could you help me?

455
00:24:01,285 --> 00:24:02,125
Merci.
Thanks.

456
00:24:02,565 --> 00:24:03,765
Tu es tellement belle.
You're so beautiful.

457
00:24:04,645 --> 00:24:06,605
Donne-moi de cette femme audacieuse et piquante.
Give me some of that bold, spicy woman.

458
00:24:09,165 --> 00:24:10,325
D'entrée de jeu.
Right off the bat.

459
00:24:11,325 --> 00:24:12,525
-Sofia ? -Oui ?
-Sofia?
-Yes?

460
00:24:12,605 --> 00:24:14,725
C'est ton tour. Tu passes.
You're next. You're up.

461
00:24:14,805 --> 00:24:16,485
-Mélanie a terminé. -Mélanie ?
-Mélanie's done.
-Mélanie?

462
00:24:17,365 --> 00:24:18,965
Mélanie Meyer. L'actrice.
Mélanie Meyer. The actress.

463
00:24:19,565 --> 00:24:22,365
-Oui. « Meilleur Espoir Féminin. » -C'est elle.
-Yes. "Most Promising Actress."
-That's the one.

464
00:24:25,725 --> 00:24:26,685
Tu le savais.
You knew.

465
00:24:26,765 --> 00:24:27,965
Je te jure, non.
I swear, I didn't.

466
00:24:28,045 --> 00:24:30,325
Je passe après la fille qui m'a pris le César ?
So I go after the girl
who beat me to the César?

467
00:24:30,605 --> 00:24:32,645
Je vais toujours arriver deuxième derrière elle ?
Am I always going to come in second
after her?

468
00:24:32,725 --> 00:24:35,325
Même son nom m'énerve, « Mélanie Meilleure ».
Even her name gets on my nerves,
"Mélanie Meilleure".

469
00:24:35,405 --> 00:24:36,245
Oui ?
Yes?

470
00:24:36,765 --> 00:24:39,205
Sofia Leprince ! Quelle joie de te voir.
Sofia Leprince! It's so great to see you.

471
00:24:39,285 --> 00:24:40,765
-Comment tu vas ? -Super !
-How are you?
-Great!

472
00:24:41,565 --> 00:24:43,445
Je te présente Camille, mon agent.
This is Camille, my agent.

473
00:24:43,525 --> 00:24:44,765
Bonjour.
Hi.

474
00:24:44,845 --> 00:24:46,085
Et toi, ça va ?
How are things with you?

475
00:24:46,165 --> 00:24:47,605
Vraiment super !
Really great!

476
00:24:47,685 --> 00:24:50,205
Au fait, félicitations pour ton César.
By the way, congratulations on your César.

477
00:24:50,285 --> 00:24:51,125
Oh, merci.
Oh, thanks.

478
00:24:51,605 --> 00:24:53,165
Être ambassadrice, c'est dingue.
Being an ambassador is insane.

479
00:24:53,245 --> 00:24:55,765
Ils te prêtent des bijoux, t'invitent à des fêtes. C'est fou.
They lend you jewelry,
invite you to parties. It's nuts.

480
00:24:57,005 --> 00:24:58,445
Tu viens ce soir ?
Are you coming tonight?

481
00:24:58,525 --> 00:24:59,765
Je ne sais pas encore.
I don't know yet.

482
00:24:59,845 --> 00:25:01,525
-On y va ensemble ? -Non.
-Are we going together?
-No.

483
00:25:03,405 --> 00:25:04,645
J'ai du travail.
I have work to do.

484
00:25:04,725 --> 00:25:06,565
Mais les soirées, c'est du travail.
But parties are work.

485
00:25:07,045 --> 00:25:09,925
Réseau. 50 % du boulot, c'est votre réseau.
Network.
50% of the job is in your network.

486
00:25:13,445 --> 00:25:14,965
On réseau ensemble ?
Want to network together?

487
00:25:21,325 --> 00:25:23,085
Qui mijote là-dedans ?
Who's stewing in there?

488
00:25:24,205 --> 00:25:26,365
M. Sarda et Mme Formain.
Mr. Sarda and Mrs. Formain.

489
00:25:26,445 --> 00:25:28,245
Oh, c'est parfait.
Oh, well, that's wonderful.

490
00:25:28,725 --> 00:25:30,645
On peut les laisser mariner jusqu'à demain ?
Can we let them simmer until tomorrow?

491
00:25:32,045 --> 00:25:33,685
Non. Je plaisante.
No. Just kidding.

492
00:25:37,765 --> 00:25:38,925
Qu'est-ce que vous faites ?
What are you doing?

493
00:25:39,885 --> 00:25:42,885
Je réserve un week-end avec ma copine.
I'm booking a weekend with my girlfriend.

494
00:25:43,485 --> 00:25:44,525
Oh, c'est sympa.
Oh, that's nice.

495
00:25:45,605 --> 00:25:46,685
Elle s'appelle comment ?
What's her name?

496
00:25:47,205 --> 00:25:48,845
Laissez tomber, elle a déjà un agent.
Forget it, she already has an agent.

497
00:25:54,245 --> 00:25:55,085
Ça va ?
Are you OK?

498
00:25:57,085 --> 00:25:57,925
Hé.
Hey.

499
00:25:59,325 --> 00:26:01,405
Vous savez que vous pouvez demander de l'aide ?
You know that you can ask for help?

500
00:26:02,245 --> 00:26:03,325
Je ne dirai rien à personne.
I won't tell anyone.

501
00:26:03,885 --> 00:26:07,005
Je dirai même que vous avez négocié un contrat pendant qu'on était bloqués.
I'll even say that you negotiated
a contract while we were stuck.

502
00:26:09,365 --> 00:26:11,285
Vous êtes vraiment décidée à ne pas m'apprécier.
You're really set on not liking me.

503
00:26:13,805 --> 00:26:15,885
On va mourir. Merde !
We're going to die. Shit!

504
00:26:15,965 --> 00:26:16,965
Non, ça va.
No, it's fine.

505
00:26:17,805 --> 00:26:19,005
Tout va bien se passer.
It's going to be OK.

506
00:26:20,485 --> 00:26:21,405
C'est bon.
It's all right.

507
00:26:23,445 --> 00:26:25,725
Vous pourriez être en mission pour Starmédia.
You could be on a mission for Starmédia.

508
00:26:26,325 --> 00:26:27,925
Envoyée ici pour nous voler nos derniers clients
Sent here to steal our last clients

509
00:26:28,005 --> 00:26:29,805
et couler l'agence définitivement.
and sink the agency for good.

510
00:26:31,045 --> 00:26:31,885
Sérieusement ?
Seriously?

511
00:26:33,165 --> 00:26:34,085
Wow, OK…
Wow, OK…

512
00:26:34,725 --> 00:26:36,325
comme un cas psychiatrique, alors ?
like a psychiatric case, then?

513
00:26:36,405 --> 00:26:39,645
Je sais, c'est pas cool de penser ça. Encore moins de le dire. Mais…
I know, it's not a cool thing to think.
Much less to say. But…

514
00:26:41,925 --> 00:26:44,165
C'est mignon quand vous essayez d'être méchante.
It's cute when you try to be mean.

515
00:26:46,125 --> 00:26:49,765
Vous êtes le seul agent avec la réputation d'être gentil.
You're the only agent
with the reputation of being nice.

516
00:26:49,845 --> 00:26:50,845
Oui, je sais, oui.
Yes, I know, yes.

517
00:26:51,405 --> 00:26:53,405
Je commence à en avoir marre.
I'm starting to be fed up with it.

518
00:26:53,885 --> 00:26:55,805
J'ai beau essayer de jouer les méchants…
No matter how hard I try
to be the bad guy…

519
00:26:56,765 --> 00:26:57,725
Ça ne marche pas.
It doesn't work.

520
00:26:58,805 --> 00:27:02,365
Ça fait rire les gens et ils me trouvent encore plus sympa.
It makes people laugh
and then they think I'm even nicer.

521
00:27:02,445 --> 00:27:03,405
Je comprends.
I understand.

522
00:27:04,645 --> 00:27:06,725
C'est pareil pour moi quand j'essaie d'être sympa.
The same happens to me
when I try to be nice.

523
00:27:13,125 --> 00:27:14,165
Là c'est mieux.
Now it's better.

524
00:27:14,245 --> 00:27:15,245
Oh, super !
Oh, great!

525
00:27:17,045 --> 00:27:17,885
Voilà…
There…

526
00:27:25,285 --> 00:27:26,125
Oh, pardon.
Oh, sorry.

527
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:27,605
Merci.
Thanks.

528
00:27:35,325 --> 00:27:37,405
Je peux parler à Colette, s'il vous plaît ?
Can I talk to Colette, please?

529
00:27:37,885 --> 00:27:39,405
Andréa ? C'est toi ?
Andréa? Is that you?

530
00:27:39,485 --> 00:27:43,245
Je sais que vous vous êtes revues, alors si elle est là, passe-la-moi.
I know you saw each other again,
so if she's there, put her on.

531
00:27:43,805 --> 00:27:44,725
Elle est partie ?
She left?

532
00:27:44,805 --> 00:27:46,165
Non, arrête.
No, stop it.

533
00:27:46,245 --> 00:27:47,885
Eva. Ne me mens pas, ou--
Eva. Don't lie to me, or--

534
00:27:47,965 --> 00:27:50,205
Ou quoi ? Tu vas rappliquer et tout saccager chez moi ?
Or what? You'll come over
and tear my place apart?

535
00:27:50,805 --> 00:27:53,845
Si j'avais réussi à la récupérer, je l'aurais crié sur les toits.
If I'd managed to get her back
I'd be shouting it from the rooftops.

536
00:27:56,205 --> 00:27:57,205
Ça fait combien de temps ?
How long has it been?

537
00:27:58,165 --> 00:27:59,245
Vingt-quatre heures.
Twenty-four hours.

538
00:27:59,725 --> 00:28:01,005
C'est rien.
That's nothing.

539
00:28:01,605 --> 00:28:03,965
Fais-lui confiance. Elle va se manifester.
Have faith in her. She'll be in touch.

540
00:28:08,325 --> 00:28:10,045
Colet-- Ah, José.
Colet-- Ah, José.

541
00:28:10,125 --> 00:28:11,005
Andréa !
Andréa!

542
00:28:11,085 --> 00:28:12,565
Qu'est-ce que tu fais là ?
What are you doing here?

543
00:28:13,285 --> 00:28:14,445
Oh, merde, écoute.
Oh, fuck, listen.

544
00:28:14,525 --> 00:28:16,565
Ça fait une éternité que je me suis pas senti aussi bien.
I haven't felt this good in ages.

545
00:28:17,285 --> 00:28:19,245
-Oh, merde, t'es bourré. -Non !
-Oh, shit, you're drunk.
-No!

546
00:28:19,325 --> 00:28:21,325
OK, ça fait une éternité que j'ai pas été aussi bourré.
OK, I haven't been this drunk in ages.

547
00:28:21,405 --> 00:28:24,405
Mais quelle nuit, Andréa ! T'as pas idée !
But what a night, Andréa!
You have no idea!

548
00:28:24,485 --> 00:28:26,725
-C'était la nuit la plus folle ! -S'il te plaît.
-It was the craziest night!
-Please.

549
00:28:26,805 --> 00:28:27,805
Calme-toi.
Tone it down.

550
00:28:27,885 --> 00:28:29,605
-Le bébé dort. -Ta fille ?
-The baby is sleeping.
- Your daughter?

551
00:28:29,685 --> 00:28:31,645
Je ne l'ai jamais vue. Je peux aller jeter un œil ?
I've never seen her. Can I go take a peek?

552
00:28:31,725 --> 00:28:32,765
Juste pour la voir.
Just to see her.

553
00:28:32,845 --> 00:28:33,805
-OK. -Elle dort !
-OK.
-She's sleeping!

554
00:28:33,885 --> 00:28:35,525
Colette est revenue ?
Did Colette come back?

555
00:28:35,605 --> 00:28:37,485
-C'est José ! -José, allez !
-It's José!
- José, come on!

556
00:28:38,165 --> 00:28:39,445
Merde, pardon.
Shit, sorry.

557
00:28:39,525 --> 00:28:41,725
Hé, regarde-moi ?
Hey, look at me?

558
00:28:41,805 --> 00:28:45,085
T'es magnifique, sérieusement. Rien qu'à te regarder, ça me redonne la pêche.
You're gorgeous, seriously. Just
looking at you puts a spring in my step.

559
00:28:45,165 --> 00:28:46,285
Je peux venir ?
Can I come?

560
00:28:46,365 --> 00:28:48,485
Reste là. Et s'il te plaît, sois discret.
Stay here. And please keep quiet.

561
00:28:48,565 --> 00:28:50,165
OK. Je peux me servir à boire ?
OK. Can I have a drink?

562
00:28:50,245 --> 00:28:51,605
Ouais, sers-toi.
Yeah, help yourself.

563
00:28:52,245 --> 00:28:55,525
Pendant des années, j'étais obsédé par l'idée de travailler avec les plus grands.
For years, I was obsessed
with idea of working with the greatest.

564
00:28:55,605 --> 00:28:58,645
Depardieu, Dujardin, Deneuve…
Depardieu, Dujardin, Deneuve…

565
00:28:58,725 --> 00:29:00,405
Tu t'es arrêté au D dans l'annuaire ?
Did you stop at D in the phone book?

566
00:29:01,285 --> 00:29:05,125
Touché. Donc je voulais faire partie de la grande famille du cinéma, mais…
Touché. So I wanted to be
a part of the big family of cinema, but…

567
00:29:05,565 --> 00:29:07,645
Après avoir essuyé tellement de refus,
After being rejected so many times,

568
00:29:07,725 --> 00:29:10,845
j'ai compris que je devais aussi créer ma propre famille.
I understood that I also need
to create my own family.

569
00:29:10,925 --> 00:29:13,885
Bien sûr, tourner avec des stars ou décrocher un César, c'est génial,
Sure, shooting with stars
or winning a César rocks,

570
00:29:13,965 --> 00:29:17,845
mais depuis que je travaille avec des acteurs qui ont la même énergie, énorme différence.
but since I've started working with actors
with the same energy, huge difference.

571
00:29:18,245 --> 00:29:20,325
On se soutient, on écrit ensemble,
We have each other's backs,
we write together,

572
00:29:20,405 --> 00:29:22,365
on partage les infos sur les castings.
we share info on auditions.

573
00:29:22,445 --> 00:29:24,285
Ça change la vie.
It's a life-changer.

574
00:29:24,365 --> 00:29:26,245
Wow. Ça ressemble à un rêve.
Wow. It sounds like a dream.

575
00:29:26,325 --> 00:29:28,605
Alors rêvons ensemble ! Travaillons sur un projet,
Then let's dream together!
Let's work on a project,

576
00:29:28,685 --> 00:29:29,685
j'adore ton énergie.
I love your energy.

577
00:29:29,765 --> 00:29:30,725
Moi aussi !
I do too!

578
00:29:30,805 --> 00:29:32,205
Je veux dire, j'adore ton énergie.
I mean, I love your energy.

579
00:29:32,285 --> 00:29:33,885
-Attends, stop. -Quoi ?
-Hold on, wait.
-What?

580
00:29:34,405 --> 00:29:35,885
Il te manque une boucle d'oreille.
You're missing an earing.

581
00:29:35,965 --> 00:29:37,485
-Non… -Si.
-No…
-Yeah.

582
00:29:38,125 --> 00:29:38,965
Elle est tombée.
It fell.

583
00:29:39,045 --> 00:29:41,805
C'est nul. C'est ta première sortie avec des bijoux empruntés.
That sucks. It's your first night out
with borrowed jewels.

584
00:29:41,885 --> 00:29:43,645
Qu'est-ce que je fais ? Ce sont des diamants.
What should I do? They're diamonds.

585
00:29:43,725 --> 00:29:46,245
T'inquiète pas. Demande à ton agent de gérer ça.
Don't worry. Ask your agent to handle it.

586
00:29:46,325 --> 00:29:47,765
Mais c'est de ma faute.
But it's my own fault.

587
00:29:47,845 --> 00:29:50,965
Ils sont là aussi pour les moments difficiles, pas seulement pour prendre un verre.
They're also here for the rough times,
not just to go out for drinks.

588
00:29:54,285 --> 00:29:55,245
T'inquiète pas.
Don't worry.

589
00:29:55,325 --> 00:29:56,205
Viens.
Come.

590
00:29:56,805 --> 00:29:58,245
-Merci, Camille. -OK.
-Thank you, Camille.
-OK.

591
00:29:58,325 --> 00:29:59,645
Le mec connaît mon prénom.
The guy knows my name.

592
00:30:00,205 --> 00:30:02,845
-Ben, j'ai demandé à ton amie, ouais. -Ah bon ?
-Well, I asked your friend, yeah.
-You did?

593
00:30:02,925 --> 00:30:04,205
-Ouais. -T'es curieux, toi.
-Yeah.
-You're inquisitive.

594
00:30:04,965 --> 00:30:06,525
Je sais ce que je veux, c'est tout.
I know what I want is all.

595
00:30:07,365 --> 00:30:09,325
J'ai failli ne pas venir ce soir.
I almost didn't come tonight.

596
00:30:09,405 --> 00:30:11,965
J'étais crevé, mais je ne regrette pas une seconde.
I was beat,
but I don't regret it for a minute.

597
00:30:13,125 --> 00:30:14,725
Sinon je ne t'aurais pas rencontrée.
Or I wouldn't have met you.

598
00:30:18,445 --> 00:30:20,765
-Je peux être franc avec toi ? -Vas-y.
-Can I be straight with you?
-Go ahead.

599
00:30:21,645 --> 00:30:23,245
Je pourrais venir chez toi ?
Could I come to your place?

600
00:30:23,845 --> 00:30:24,685
OK, je vois.
OK, I see.

601
00:30:25,685 --> 00:30:26,685
Non, j'étais maladroit ?
No, was I clumsy?

602
00:30:26,765 --> 00:30:28,005
-Non. -Si, je le sens.
-No.
-Yeah, I can feel it.

603
00:30:28,085 --> 00:30:29,085
Non, je suis désolé.
No, I'm sorry.

604
00:30:29,165 --> 00:30:30,165
C'est très gentil.
It's very sweet.

605
00:30:30,245 --> 00:30:31,085
OK.
OK.

606
00:30:31,845 --> 00:30:34,965
-Maintenant ? -Oh non, on peut attendre les heures de bureau.
-Right now?
-Oh no, we can wait for office hours.

607
00:30:35,405 --> 00:30:37,925
Signer avec ASK, c'est un rêve de toujours, je peux attendre.
It's a life-long dream
to sign with ASK, so I can wait.

608
00:30:42,445 --> 00:30:44,685
-Elle dort enfin. -Je suis désolée.
-She's finally asleep.
-I'm sorry.

609
00:30:47,765 --> 00:30:49,285
Alors, qu'est-ce que tu as fait ce soir ?
So, what did you do tonight?

610
00:30:49,365 --> 00:30:50,285
J'étais avec Laurence.
I was with Laurence.

611
00:30:51,005 --> 00:30:54,365
Quelle femme, Andréa, tu as aucune idée ! Quelle nuit !
What a woman, Andréa,
you have no idea! What a night!

612
00:30:54,445 --> 00:30:56,205
-Et toi… ? -On a parlé !
-And you…?
-We talked!

613
00:30:56,285 --> 00:30:57,605
Des heures. Écoute,
For hours. Listen,

614
00:30:57,685 --> 00:31:00,685
j'ai fait tout ce que tu m'as dit. D'une chose à l'autre,
I did everything you told me to.
One thing leading to another,

615
00:31:00,765 --> 00:31:02,765
on se retrouvait comme à 20 ans.
we were hitting it off again
like we were 20.

616
00:31:03,325 --> 00:31:05,525
Rien n'a changé. On avait de nouveau 25 ans.
Nothing's changed. We were 25 again.

617
00:31:05,605 --> 00:31:07,965
Puis je l'ai emmenée dans un resto gitan.
Then I took her to a gypsy restaurant.

618
00:31:08,045 --> 00:31:10,365
J'ai pas perdu la main, merde. J'ai même fait
I've still got it, damn it. I even did

619
00:31:10,445 --> 00:31:11,605
un grand écart et je me suis fait mal au…
a jazz split and hurt my…

620
00:31:11,685 --> 00:31:13,205
-José… -Oui, bon, d'accord.
-José…
-Yeah, all right.

621
00:31:14,885 --> 00:31:17,125
-Et alors ? -Et ben, je…
-And?
-And, well, I…

622
00:31:18,845 --> 00:31:21,525
Je lui ai dit de me rejoindre demain,
I told her to meet me tomorrow,

623
00:31:22,605 --> 00:31:25,245
demain soir à l'hôtel
tomorrow night at the hotel

624
00:31:25,325 --> 00:31:27,565
du rendez-vous qui n'a jamais eu lieu, chambre 10.
from the date that never was, room 10.

625
00:31:29,005 --> 00:31:30,885
-Mais pourquoi t'as fait ça ? -Pourquoi ?
-But why did you do that?
-Why?

626
00:31:31,445 --> 00:31:33,525
Parce que c'est revenu comme avant.
Because it's back like it was before.

627
00:31:33,605 --> 00:31:35,085
Mais en mieux. C'est le vrai amour.
But even better. It's true love.

628
00:31:35,165 --> 00:31:37,445
Mais, José, t'es pas encore marié ?
But, José, aren't you still married?

629
00:31:37,525 --> 00:31:38,365
Ben, si.
Well, yeah.

630
00:31:41,405 --> 00:31:42,645
C'est un coup de foudre.
It's love at first sight.

631
00:31:45,645 --> 00:31:47,765
Oh, merde. T'as frappé ?
Oh, fuck. You knocked?

632
00:31:49,485 --> 00:31:51,685
Non ? Il y a vingt ans ?
Didn't you? Twenty years ago?

633
00:31:52,645 --> 00:31:55,445
T'as frappé à cette porte et elle n'a jamais répondu.
You knocked on that door
and she never answered.

634
00:31:58,605 --> 00:32:00,165
Ça t'a brisé le cœur et c'est pour ça
It broke your heart and that's why

635
00:32:00,245 --> 00:32:02,805
que t'as disjoncté en la voyant. Et là, ça revient.
you flipped when you saw her.
And now, it's back again.

636
00:32:08,205 --> 00:32:11,045
C'est mieux cette fois. On est fous amoureux et…
It's better this time.
We're crazy in love and…

637
00:32:11,845 --> 00:32:12,965
J'ai envie d'y croire.
I want to believe in it.

638
00:32:15,125 --> 00:32:16,845
Comme au cinéma, mais dans la vraie vie.
Like in the movies, but in real life.

639
00:32:17,325 --> 00:32:18,205
Tu comprends ?
Can you understand?

640
00:32:19,165 --> 00:32:21,525
Toi, mon agent ? Bref…
You, my agent? Anyway…

641
00:32:22,645 --> 00:32:23,845
Assez parlé de moi.
Enough of me.

642
00:32:23,925 --> 00:32:27,405
-T'as assez de problèmes. -Tu vas où ? Assieds-toi.
-You've got enough problems.
-Where are you going? Sit down.

643
00:32:27,485 --> 00:32:28,645
Tu tournes demain.
You're shooting tomorrow.

644
00:32:29,365 --> 00:32:31,445
Je peux pas te laisser partir dans cet état.
I can't let you go in this state.

645
00:32:31,525 --> 00:32:34,565
Dors ici. L'assistant de production viendra te chercher ici.
Sleep here. The unit manager
will come pick you up here.

646
00:32:34,645 --> 00:32:36,805
Je dois me lever tôt demain, j'ai la garde partagée.
I gotta get up early tomorrow,
I'm co-parenting.

647
00:32:36,885 --> 00:32:37,765
La garde partagée ?
Co-parenting?

648
00:32:37,845 --> 00:32:40,005
À la crèche des Coccinelles, c'est un concept.
At the Ladybugs Daycare Center,
it's a concept.

649
00:32:40,085 --> 00:32:41,965
Alors je te réveillerai en partant. Marché conclu ?
So I'll wake you up when I leave. Deal?

650
00:32:42,045 --> 00:32:43,165
Je vais chercher des draps.
I'll get some sheets.

651
00:32:43,885 --> 00:32:45,165
-Andréa ? -Oui ?
-Andréa?
-Yes?

652
00:32:45,645 --> 00:32:46,485
Merci.
Thanks.

653
00:32:50,165 --> 00:32:51,005
Oh, merde.
Oh, fuck.

654
00:33:14,005 --> 00:33:15,605
Putain.
Oh, shit.

655
00:33:15,685 --> 00:33:16,685
José ?
José?

656
00:33:18,845 --> 00:33:20,845
Il faut te lever, on est en retard.
You have to wake up, we're late.

657
00:33:20,925 --> 00:33:21,765
José…
José…

658
00:33:26,205 --> 00:33:28,325
-Allô ? -Je viens chercher José.
-Hello?
-I'm here to pick up José.

659
00:33:28,405 --> 00:33:30,165
Je le cherche aussi.
I'm looking for him too.

660
00:33:30,245 --> 00:33:32,045
Mais il est parti, il n'est plus là.
But he's gone, he isn't here.

661
00:33:32,125 --> 00:33:34,405
-Il n'est pas avec toi ? -Ben, non.
-He's not with you?
-Well, no.

662
00:33:35,805 --> 00:33:37,285
Je te rappelle, OK ?
I'll call you back, OK?

663
00:33:37,925 --> 00:33:40,005
Mon cœur, il faut te réveiller.
Sweetheart, you've got to wake up.

664
00:33:40,085 --> 00:33:41,565
On est en retard pour la crèche.
We're late for daycare.

665
00:33:43,165 --> 00:33:44,005
Flora ?
Flora?

666
00:33:52,965 --> 00:33:54,205
Andréa, ça va ?
Andréa, you're OK?

667
00:33:54,965 --> 00:33:56,685
Oh, mon bébé, mon bébé…
Oh, my baby, my baby…

668
00:34:01,045 --> 00:34:02,525
T'es folle.
You're insane.

669
00:34:02,605 --> 00:34:05,285
Attends, tout va bien, allez, calme-toi.
Hold on, everything's fine, hey relax.

670
00:34:05,365 --> 00:34:07,285
J'ai laissé un mot. T'as pas vu ?
I left a note. You didn't see it?

671
00:34:07,365 --> 00:34:10,485
Ils ont appelé ce matin, je voulais pas te réveiller.
They called this morning,
I didn't want to wake you up.

672
00:34:10,565 --> 00:34:11,685
Et maintenant… Regarde !
And now… Look!

673
00:34:11,765 --> 00:34:12,845
Princesse Joues-rebondies.
Princess Chubby-cheeks.

674
00:34:13,765 --> 00:34:15,684
Je me suis retrouvée ici avec tous les petits bébés.
I wound up here
with all the little babies.

675
00:34:16,125 --> 00:34:17,085
Elle est où, la co-maman ?
Where's the co-mom?

676
00:34:17,684 --> 00:34:19,805
-Qui ? -La dame qui s'occupe des bébés.
-Who?
-The lady who takes care of the babies.

677
00:34:19,885 --> 00:34:21,164
Ah oui, Capu. Capu ?
Oh, yes, Capu. Capu?

678
00:34:21,644 --> 00:34:23,325
Elle s'appelle Capucine.
Her name is Capucine.

679
00:34:23,405 --> 00:34:25,925
-Là, là, regarde. -Super, Andréa. Génial.
-Here, here, look.
-Great, Andréa. Awesome.

680
00:34:26,765 --> 00:34:27,965
-Tout va bien ? -Non !
-Everything OK?
-No!

681
00:34:28,045 --> 00:34:30,045
C'est un enlèvement d'enfant ce que t'as fait.
It's child abduction what you did.

682
00:34:30,125 --> 00:34:31,445
-Quoi ? -Si, si !
-What?
-That's right!

683
00:34:31,525 --> 00:34:33,365
Non. Allez… Hé, calme-toi,
No. Come on… Hey, relax,

684
00:34:33,445 --> 00:34:35,365
respire. Tout va bien.
breathe. Everything's fine.

685
00:34:35,845 --> 00:34:37,845
T'es à bout. Respire.
You're totally on edge. Breathe.

686
00:34:37,925 --> 00:34:39,285
C'est la faute de qui, ça ?
Whose fault is that?

687
00:34:39,365 --> 00:34:40,445
Ben, de Colette.
Well, Colette's.

688
00:34:40,925 --> 00:34:42,644
Regarde, on est zen.
Look, we're chill.

689
00:34:43,285 --> 00:34:44,445
On est détendus.
We're relaxed.

690
00:34:44,965 --> 00:34:46,525
Pas toi. Regarde. Ça, c'est toi !
Not you. Look. That's you!

691
00:34:46,605 --> 00:34:48,005
Princesse Joues-rebondies.
Princess Chubby-cheeks.

692
00:34:48,085 --> 00:34:49,765
Une voiture t'attend
A car's waiting for you

693
00:34:49,845 --> 00:34:51,204
avec l'unité de direction à l'intérieur.
with the manager unit inside.

694
00:34:51,285 --> 00:34:53,765
Tu vas monter. Je vais t'accompagner.
You're going to get in.
I'm going to come with you.

695
00:34:53,845 --> 00:34:55,164
-T'entends ? -Oui.
-You hear?
-Yes.

696
00:34:56,244 --> 00:34:58,445
J'ai un truc à régler.
I have something to sort out.

697
00:34:58,525 --> 00:35:00,005
Comment ça ? Non.
What do you mean? No.

698
00:35:00,085 --> 00:35:01,644
Et la coparentalité ?
What about the co-parenting?

699
00:35:01,724 --> 00:35:03,605
Ben… On continue comme ça.
Well… Let's just keep it up.

700
00:35:03,685 --> 00:35:06,005
Toi tu t'occupes des petits, qui t'adorent,
You take care of the little kids,
who love you,

701
00:35:06,085 --> 00:35:08,565
et moi je m'occupe du grand. OK ?
and I take care of the big kid. OK?

702
00:35:09,085 --> 00:35:11,085
-Super, merci, « Capu ». -OK…
-Great, thanks, "Capu."
-OK…

703
00:35:11,165 --> 00:35:12,605
José. On y va.
José. Let's go.

704
00:35:12,685 --> 00:35:13,725
Ouais. Ouais, ouais.
Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

705
00:35:13,805 --> 00:35:15,565
Tiens, regarde, fais attention, parce que…
Here, look, careful, because…

706
00:35:16,045 --> 00:35:18,765
Elle retient un peu son souffle. Je crois qu'elle est constipée.
She's kind of holding her breath.
I think she's constipated.

707
00:35:18,845 --> 00:35:19,805
-OK. -D'accord ?
-OK.
-All right?

708
00:35:19,885 --> 00:35:20,725
Super.
Great.

709
00:35:20,805 --> 00:35:22,325
-OK, au revoir. -Ouais.
-OK, bye.
-Yeah.

710
00:35:24,325 --> 00:35:30,085
Pieds dans l'axe des hanches. Inspirez et bloquez, et expirez.
Feet lined up with the hips.
Inhale and hold your breath, and out.

711
00:35:34,165 --> 00:35:36,925
Inspirez, bloquez, et respirez.
Inhale, hold, and breathe.

712
00:35:39,685 --> 00:35:41,685
OK, j'ai compris.
OK, I get it.

713
00:35:41,765 --> 00:35:43,325
Attends, je le fais pour moi.
Wait, I'm doing it for me.

714
00:35:44,525 --> 00:35:46,445
-Alex, c'est ton tour. -OK.
-Alex, you're up.
-OK.

715
00:35:47,165 --> 00:35:48,525
-Tu lui souffles les réponses ? -Non.
-Are you cuing her in?
-No.

716
00:35:48,605 --> 00:35:49,685
-Si ! -Oui ou non ?
-Yes!
-Yes or no?

717
00:35:49,765 --> 00:35:51,085
-Si ! -Allez, tout le monde.
-Yes!
-Let's go kiddos.

718
00:35:51,165 --> 00:35:52,885
-OK. -On y va. Dépêchez-vous.
-OK.
-Time to go. Chop-chop.

719
00:35:53,445 --> 00:35:54,965
Bonjour ! Alex, c'est ça ?
Hello! Alex, is it?

720
00:35:55,045 --> 00:35:56,685
-Oui. -Vous pouvez poser vos affaires ici.
-Yes.
-You can put your things here.

721
00:35:57,325 --> 00:36:00,365
Vous avez un bon agent, Alex. Il a insisté pour vous donner une autre chance.
You've a good agent, Alex.
He insisted on giving you another chance.

722
00:36:00,445 --> 00:36:02,485
Hervé. Je suis son agent.
Hervé. I'm her agent.

723
00:36:02,565 --> 00:36:05,525
Je suis un grand admirateur de votre travail, madame Donzelli.
I'm a great admirer of your work,
Mrs. Donzelli.

724
00:36:05,605 --> 00:36:08,325
Appelez-moi Valérie, s'il vous plaît. Je ne suis pas Nicole Garcia.
Please, call me Valérie.
I'm not Nicole Garcia.

725
00:36:09,605 --> 00:36:10,605
J'aimerais l'être, mais…
I'd like to be, but…

726
00:36:11,325 --> 00:36:12,565
On est bons ? Prêts ?
Are we good? Ready?

727
00:36:12,645 --> 00:36:14,165
-OK, oui. -Ça va ?
-OK, yes.
-All right?

728
00:36:14,245 --> 00:36:15,885
-Victoria ? -On tourne.
-Victoria?
-Rolling.

729
00:36:15,965 --> 00:36:17,405
Quand vous voulez.
Whenever you're ready.

730
00:36:18,485 --> 00:36:19,445
Je n'y vais pas.
I'm not going.

731
00:36:19,525 --> 00:36:21,125
Tu n'y vas pas ?
You're not going?

732
00:36:21,685 --> 00:36:23,365
Il faut y aller, maman va rentrer bientôt.
We have to go, mom will be home soon.

733
00:36:23,445 --> 00:36:26,005
Et alors ? On devrait peut-être voir maman d'abord si on--
So? Maybe we should see mom first if we--

734
00:36:26,085 --> 00:36:28,325
Stop ! Non. C'est pas juste.
Stop! No. It's not right.

735
00:36:28,885 --> 00:36:30,605
-Super. Je le savais. -Non, c'est pas toi.
-Great. I knew it.
-No, it's not you.

736
00:36:30,685 --> 00:36:32,205
C'est la scène. Je l'ai vue toute la journée,
It's the scene. I saw it all day,

737
00:36:32,285 --> 00:36:34,685
je n'en peux plus.
I can't stand it anymore.

738
00:36:35,565 --> 00:36:36,605
On va improviser.
Let's do an improv.

739
00:36:37,885 --> 00:36:40,085
-Je ne sais pas comment faire. -Il n'y a rien à faire.
-I don't know how.
-There's nothing to do.

740
00:36:40,165 --> 00:36:43,165
Suis ce qui vient, quand ça vient.
Go along with whatever comes to you,
whenever it comes to you.

741
00:36:43,245 --> 00:36:45,445
Laisse-toi aller, improvise. OK ?
Just let yourself go, improvise. OK?

742
00:36:46,005 --> 00:36:47,565
Hervé va te lancer.
Hervé will start you off.

743
00:36:47,645 --> 00:36:50,125
Hervé, tu vas la surprendre.
Hervé, you're going to surprise her.

744
00:36:51,485 --> 00:36:53,805
Tu la plaques au sol. OK ?
You pin her down to the ground. OK?

745
00:36:53,885 --> 00:36:56,965
On essaie. Tu vas t'en sortir. Prêts ?
Let's give it a try.
You'll be fine. Ready?

746
00:36:58,725 --> 00:36:59,565
On est bons ?
Are we good?

747
00:36:59,645 --> 00:37:00,685
-On tourne. -Action !
-Rolling.
-Action!

748
00:37:05,085 --> 00:37:07,485
Je suis tellement heureuse. C'est beau !
I'm so happy. It's beautiful!

749
00:37:07,565 --> 00:37:08,405
C'était…
It was…

750
00:37:09,725 --> 00:37:11,245
dingue ! C'était intense !
insane! It was intense!

751
00:37:11,325 --> 00:37:13,965
Wow. Je veux recommencer.
Wow. I want to do it again.

752
00:37:14,045 --> 00:37:15,445
Je veux faire ça toute ma vie.
I want to do it my whole life.

753
00:37:15,925 --> 00:37:18,045
Je veux que tu le fasses toute ta vie aussi.
I want you to do it your whole life
as well.

754
00:37:18,125 --> 00:37:19,245
Merci.
Thanks.

755
00:37:19,325 --> 00:37:22,365
Merci d'être aussi agaçant, aussi tordu.
Thanks for being so annoying, so twisted.

756
00:37:24,205 --> 00:37:25,285
C'est mon travail.
It's my job.

757
00:37:27,765 --> 00:37:29,805
On peut aller aussi vite sur le suivant ?
Can we be as quick on the next?

758
00:37:30,125 --> 00:37:31,245
-Andréa. -Comment ça va ?
-Andréa.
-How's it going?

759
00:37:31,325 --> 00:37:33,165
-José est en grande forme ! -Oui.
-José is in great shape!
-Yes.

760
00:37:33,245 --> 00:37:34,205
En grande forme.
In great shape.

761
00:37:36,645 --> 00:37:37,965
Pour les scènes en extérieur…
For outside scenes…

762
00:37:41,805 --> 00:37:43,525
Tu vas le voir ce soir ?
Are you going to meet him tonight?

763
00:37:45,005 --> 00:37:47,125
En effet, la prudence n'est pas ton fort.
Indeed,
treading carefully isn't your thing.

764
00:37:47,605 --> 00:37:49,045
Je ne vais pas lâcher.
I'm not going to let up.

765
00:37:49,565 --> 00:37:50,925
Alors, tu y vas ?
So, are you?

766
00:37:55,805 --> 00:37:57,205
En quoi ça te regarde ?
What is it to you?

767
00:37:58,325 --> 00:38:00,525
Tu prends aussi 10 % sur sa vie sexuelle ?
Do you also take 10% on his sex life?

768
00:38:01,565 --> 00:38:03,925
Non, mais je dois être impliqué dans ses affaires de cœur.
No, but I have to be involved
in his heart matters.

769
00:38:04,005 --> 00:38:07,445
Tu le rends heureux et c'est merveilleux. J'adore voir José sur un nuage.
You make him happy and that's wonderful.
I love seeing José walking on air.

770
00:38:08,525 --> 00:38:10,605
Mais quand il tombe, c'est moi qui le ramasse.
But when he falls,
I'm the one picking him up.

771
00:38:10,685 --> 00:38:12,765
Et plus on monte haut, plus la chute est dure.
And the higher the soar,
the harder the fall.

772
00:38:13,565 --> 00:38:16,125
Et là, il monte très haut. Dans l'espace.
And now he's soaring very high.
Up in space.

773
00:38:16,805 --> 00:38:17,925
Oui, je comprends.
Yes, I understand.

774
00:38:18,485 --> 00:38:20,125
Mais José est grand.
But José's a big boy.

775
00:38:20,205 --> 00:38:22,125
On a parlé, et j'ai été très clair.
We talked, and I was very clear.

776
00:38:22,205 --> 00:38:23,205
C'est léger.
It's light.

777
00:38:23,765 --> 00:38:24,845
Pas de prise de tête.
There's no hassle.

778
00:38:28,605 --> 00:38:29,845
Il ne joue pas.
He's not playing.

779
00:38:30,045 --> 00:38:32,405
Un homme amoureux t'attend dans cet hôtel.
A man in love will be waiting for you
in that hotel.

780
00:38:34,485 --> 00:38:36,285
Donc si tu n'y vas pas,
So if you're not going,

781
00:38:37,285 --> 00:38:39,405
Préviens-le. D'accord ?
let him know. All right?

782
00:38:40,365 --> 00:38:41,965
Tout le monde en position !
Everyone get into position!

783
00:38:42,965 --> 00:38:43,965
Tout le monde est prêt ?
Is everybody ready?

784
00:38:51,005 --> 00:38:52,365
L'agneau est parfait.
The lamb looks perfect.

785
00:38:52,965 --> 00:38:53,805
Mathias…
Mathias…

786
00:38:54,525 --> 00:38:57,645
-Tu crois que sa femme va m'aimer ? -Sans aucun doute.
-Do you think his wife will like me?
-No doubt.

787
00:39:01,725 --> 00:39:02,565
Et Catherine ?
And Catherine?

788
00:39:03,285 --> 00:39:04,645
Elle aurait servi de l'agneau ?
She'd have served lamb?

789
00:39:05,565 --> 00:39:06,925
Catherine, c'est Catherine.
Catherine is Catherine.

790
00:39:07,005 --> 00:39:09,645
Toi, c'est toi. Arrête de te comparer.
You're you. Stop comparing yourself.

791
00:39:13,165 --> 00:39:14,165
C'est toi que j'aime.
It's you I love.

792
00:39:16,245 --> 00:39:17,685
Tout va bien se passer.
Everything will be fine.

793
00:39:22,645 --> 00:39:23,485
Alors…
So…

794
00:39:24,165 --> 00:39:26,885
dis-moi, quels sont ses centres d'intérêt ?
tell me, what are her areas of interest?

795
00:39:26,965 --> 00:39:28,965
-Elle est très écolo. -Oui…
-She's very pro-environment.
-Yes…

796
00:39:29,045 --> 00:39:30,645
Les espèces en voie d'extinction,
Endangered species,

797
00:39:30,725 --> 00:39:33,565
la cruauté dans les abattoirs, ce genre de choses.
in slaughterhouse cruelty,
that kind of thing.

798
00:39:34,525 --> 00:39:36,445
Attends, tu me dis ça maintenant ?
Hold on, you're telling me now?

799
00:39:44,325 --> 00:39:45,525
Qu'est-ce que tu fais ?
What are you doing?

800
00:39:46,005 --> 00:39:48,045
Je ne peux pas lui servir le cadavre d'un animal mort !
I can't serve her
the corpse of a dead animal!

801
00:39:48,125 --> 00:39:50,085
Mais c'est un cadavre à 100 euros !
But it's a 100-euro corpse!

802
00:39:51,845 --> 00:39:53,965
Franchement, bravo Mathias.
Honestly, well done, Mathias.

803
00:39:54,045 --> 00:39:55,765
Qu'est-ce qu'on va manger maintenant ?
What are we going to eat now?

804
00:39:55,845 --> 00:39:58,645
Je sais pas. Je vais faire plus de légumes. Et du riz en plus.
I don't know. I'll make more vegetables.
And some extra rice.

805
00:39:58,725 --> 00:40:00,565
Et on va servir beaucoup de vin. Voilà.
And we'll serve a lot of wine. There.

806
00:40:02,365 --> 00:40:04,125
Attends, il faut que je me rattrape.
Hold on, I have to catch up.

807
00:40:04,205 --> 00:40:06,485
-C'est quoi les espèces en danger ? -Quel gâchis.
-What are the endangered species?
-What a waste.

808
00:40:06,565 --> 00:40:07,405
Mon Dieu.
Oh, my God.

809
00:40:07,965 --> 00:40:09,885
Les rhinocéros, il en reste ou c'est fini ?
Rhinos,
are there any left or is that over?

810
00:40:09,965 --> 00:40:11,645
Comment veux-tu que je le sache ?
How should I know?

811
00:40:13,045 --> 00:40:14,405
Bonsoir.
Hi, good evening.

812
00:40:14,485 --> 00:40:15,845
-Bonsoir ! -Entrez.
-Good evening!
-Come in.

813
00:40:15,925 --> 00:40:17,405
-Allez, Roméo. -Ça alors !
-Come on, Romeo.
-How about that!

814
00:40:17,485 --> 00:40:19,805
Oui, désolée, je vous avais pas prévenus. Tenez.
Yes, sorry, I didn't warn you. Here.

815
00:40:20,605 --> 00:40:21,605
Oh, magnifique.
Oh, wonderful.

816
00:40:21,685 --> 00:40:23,405
-Comment allez… -Salut ! Je suis Claire.
-How do you?
-Hi! I'm Claire.

817
00:40:23,485 --> 00:40:25,205
-Noémie. -Vous n'avez pas de chat, j'espère ?
-Noémie.
-You don't have a cat, do you?

818
00:40:25,685 --> 00:40:27,925
-Sinon on aurait dû l'enfermer. -Oh là là.
-Otherwise we'd have had to lock it up.
-Oh my.

819
00:40:28,005 --> 00:40:29,885
Quelle belle doublure.
What a gorgeous lining.

820
00:40:29,965 --> 00:40:31,205
Oh, merci.
Oh, thank you.

821
00:40:31,285 --> 00:40:34,565
Les couleurs me rappellent la salamandre géante de Chine.
The colors remind me
of the Chinese giant salamander.

822
00:40:34,645 --> 00:40:35,805
Le quoi ?
The what?

823
00:40:35,885 --> 00:40:36,845
Vous savez,
You know,

824
00:40:36,925 --> 00:40:38,645
les espèces en voie d'extinction ?
the endangered species?

825
00:40:39,645 --> 00:40:42,205
Comme le wallaby des rochers, malheureusement.
Similar in this respect
to the rock-wallaby, I'm afraid.

826
00:40:42,565 --> 00:40:45,405
Oh non, je ne m'y connais pas trop en animaux. Donc je…
Oh no, I don't know much about animals.
So I…

827
00:40:46,605 --> 00:40:47,965
Je suis désolé.
I'm sorry.

828
00:40:48,045 --> 00:40:50,125
On n'a jamais autant de silence que ça.
It doesn't get any quieter than this.

829
00:40:50,205 --> 00:40:51,885
Je voulais m'excuser
I meant to apologize

830
00:40:52,365 --> 00:40:53,405
pour hier.
about yesterday.

831
00:40:54,365 --> 00:40:56,445
Je me sens mal d'avoir été aussi maladroit.
I feel bad about being so tactless.

832
00:40:56,525 --> 00:40:57,845
Hier, quoi ?
What about yesterday?

833
00:40:58,725 --> 00:41:00,805
Quand tu as appelé, j'étais pris,
When you called, I got all tied up,

834
00:41:00,885 --> 00:41:02,805
et tu as dû mal interpréter mais--
and you must have got the wrong idea but--

835
00:41:02,885 --> 00:41:04,645
Non, je déjeunais avec Igor.
No, I was having lunch with Igor.

836
00:41:04,725 --> 00:41:06,565
Tu as dû avoir Béatrice au téléphone.
You must have had Béatrice on the phone.

837
00:41:07,125 --> 00:41:09,365
-Béatrice ? -Oui, la femme d'Igor.
-Béatrice?
-Yes, Igor's wife.

838
00:41:09,445 --> 00:41:11,205
Je le sentais. Claire, viens voir.
I could feel it. Claire. Come see.

839
00:41:14,085 --> 00:41:16,325
-C'est beau. -Regarde comme ils sont bien installés.
-It's beautiful.
-Look how they're all settled in.

840
00:41:19,405 --> 00:41:20,805
Tu savais que c'était pas sa femme !
You knew it wasn't his wife!

841
00:41:20,885 --> 00:41:23,165
C'est pour ça que je te faisais des signaux.
That's why I kept signaling to you.

842
00:41:23,245 --> 00:41:24,965
Mais ça ne veut rien dire !
But that doesn't mean anything!

843
00:41:25,045 --> 00:41:26,965
Ou peut-être : « Coucou, je fais un AVC ! »
Or perhaps:
"Yoo-hoo, I'm having a stroke!"

844
00:41:27,045 --> 00:41:28,845
Je suis sûre qu'on va passer une super soirée.
I'm sure we'll spend a great evening.

845
00:41:28,925 --> 00:41:30,405
Claire a l'air charmante.
Claire seems charming.

846
00:41:30,485 --> 00:41:32,565
Pour toi, une super soirée, c'est quand le producteur
For you, a great evening,
is when the producer

847
00:41:32,645 --> 00:41:35,245
débarque avec sa maîtresse ? Où est le respect là-dedans ?
shows up with his mistress?
Where is the respect in that?

848
00:41:35,325 --> 00:41:38,845
On n'est pas vraiment en position de faire la morale sur l'adultère.
We're in no position
to lecture people about adultery.

849
00:41:38,925 --> 00:41:40,565
Mais c'était totalement différent.
But that was totally different.

850
00:41:41,045 --> 00:41:43,085
Toi et moi, on s'est battues la coulpe.
You and I,
we pummeled our breasts with grief.

851
00:41:43,565 --> 00:41:46,045
On a pleuré dans le bain en se soûlant.
We cried in the bath while getting drunk.

852
00:41:48,285 --> 00:41:49,805
On était romantiques.
We were romantic.

853
00:42:36,805 --> 00:42:38,805
Je devrais peut-être faire du réseau,
Maybe I should do some networking,

854
00:42:38,885 --> 00:42:39,885
rencontrer des gens,
meet people,

855
00:42:39,965 --> 00:42:42,245
mais j'ai déjà 15 comédiens, dix auteurs.
but I already have 15 actors, ten writers.

856
00:42:42,325 --> 00:42:43,485
C'est beaucoup de travail.
It's a lot of work.

857
00:42:43,965 --> 00:42:47,085
Écoute, je suis très fière de toi, chérie, mais tu dois
Look, I'm very proud of you, honey,
but you need

858
00:42:47,165 --> 00:42:49,165
penser à toi.
to think of yourself.

859
00:42:49,245 --> 00:42:51,565
Le travail, c'est bien beau, mais quand même.
Work is all very well, but still.

860
00:42:51,645 --> 00:42:53,885
N'oublie pas de vivre, sinon ça sert à quoi ?
Don't forget to live,
otherwise what's the point?

861
00:42:55,085 --> 00:42:57,805
Par exemple, combien de petits amis tu as ?
For instance,
how many boyfriends do you have?

862
00:42:57,885 --> 00:42:59,605
Maman, j'ai la tête ailleurs en ce moment.
Mom, my head is elsewhere right now.

863
00:42:59,685 --> 00:43:01,445
Je ne parle pas de ta tête.
I'm not talking about your head.

864
00:43:01,525 --> 00:43:03,965
- Maman ! - Quoi ? Oh…
- Mom!
- Well, what? Oh…

865
00:43:05,085 --> 00:43:08,285
De toute façon, si c'est cette histoire de reconnaissance de paternité
Anyway, if it's this recognition
of paternity business

866
00:43:08,365 --> 00:43:10,965
qui t'embête, tu sais ce que j'en pense.
that's bothering you,
you know what I think about it.

867
00:43:11,045 --> 00:43:12,925
Pas du tout, j'y réfléchis, c'est tout.
Not at all, I'm thinking about it is all.

868
00:43:14,565 --> 00:43:17,005
Pourquoi tu es contre maintenant ? Tu rêvais que Mathias
Why are you against it now?
You dreamed about Mathias

869
00:43:17,085 --> 00:43:19,005
me reconnaisse, et là c'est une mauvaise idée ?
acknowledging me, and now it's a bad idea?

870
00:43:19,085 --> 00:43:22,405
Parce que c'est trop tard ! Il aurait dû le faire quand on avait besoin de lui.
Because it's too late!
He should have done it when we needed him.

871
00:43:22,885 --> 00:43:23,805
C'est facile
It's easy

872
00:43:23,885 --> 00:43:26,365
maintenant que tu as 15 comédiens, 20 auteurs.
now that you have 15 actors, 20 writers.

873
00:43:26,445 --> 00:43:28,045
Il croit que la paternité, ça veut dire
Does he think that fatherhood means

874
00:43:28,125 --> 00:43:30,405
signer un bout de papier quand ça lui chante ?
signing a piece of paper
when you feel like it?

875
00:43:30,485 --> 00:43:33,165
C'est moi qui ai fait tout le travail depuis 27 ans.
I am the one who did all the work
for the past 27 years.

876
00:43:33,245 --> 00:43:34,845
Ce n'est pas la question. Et de toute façon,
That's not the issue. And besides,

877
00:43:34,925 --> 00:43:38,325
t'inquiète, je ne vais pas changer de nom.
don't worry,
I'm not going to change my last name.

878
00:43:38,405 --> 00:43:40,405
Je n'y avais même pas pensé.
I'd never even considered that.

879
00:43:42,805 --> 00:43:43,805
Voilà !
Here we are!

880
00:43:44,285 --> 00:43:45,885
Un délicieux gigot d'agneau.
A delicious leg of lamb.

881
00:43:46,805 --> 00:43:49,405
- Claire, vous en voulez ? - Avec plaisir.
-Claire, would you like some?
-With pleasure.

882
00:43:49,845 --> 00:43:51,205
On ne passait pas au végétarien ?
We weren't going vegetarian?

883
00:43:51,485 --> 00:43:53,925
On n'a pas toujours ce qu'on attend.
You don't always get what you expect.

884
00:43:54,005 --> 00:43:56,685
La vie est pleine de surprises, n'est-ce pas, Igor ?
Life is full of surprises, isn't it, Igor?

885
00:43:56,765 --> 00:43:57,645
Je ne peux pas manger d'agneau.
I can't eat lamb.

886
00:43:58,285 --> 00:43:59,205
- Oh. - Non.
-Oh.
-No.

887
00:43:59,285 --> 00:44:00,445
C'est pas vrai.
It's not true.

888
00:44:00,525 --> 00:44:01,765
Non, bien sûr que non.
No, of course not.

889
00:44:01,845 --> 00:44:02,685
Vous êtes sûre ?
You're sure?

890
00:44:03,165 --> 00:44:04,605
Oui. C'était une mauvaise blague.
Yes. It was a bad joke.

891
00:44:04,685 --> 00:44:06,765
- OK. - J'adore ça. Je salive déjà.
-OK.
-I love it. I'm drooling already.

892
00:44:07,445 --> 00:44:09,165
- Je vous en sers une grande tranche ? - Oui.
-Should I serve you a big slice?
-Yes.

893
00:44:09,245 --> 00:44:10,565
- Très bien. - Merci.
-All right.
-Thank you.

894
00:44:11,605 --> 00:44:13,525
On avait dit qu'on ne parlerait pas boulot,
We said we wouldn't talk shop,

895
00:44:13,605 --> 00:44:15,605
mais j'ai des nouvelles sur le film de Beauvois.
but I have some news
about the Beauvois film.

896
00:44:15,685 --> 00:44:17,085
- Mathias ? De l'agneau ? - Non, merci.
-Mathias? Lamb?
-No, thanks.

897
00:44:17,165 --> 00:44:18,205
Juste la première tranche.
Just the first slice.

898
00:44:19,285 --> 00:44:20,125
Auteuil l'a lu.
Auteuil read it.

899
00:44:22,645 --> 00:44:24,165
Il a de sérieuses réserves.
He has some serious reservations.

900
00:44:24,245 --> 00:44:26,645
Et je suis globalement du même avis.
And I am globally on the same side.

901
00:44:27,485 --> 00:44:28,485
On peut en discuter,
We can discuss it,

902
00:44:28,565 --> 00:44:30,885
mais j'ai promis à Xavier qu'on ne toucherait pas à son scénario,
but I promised Xavier
we wouldn't touch his script,

903
00:44:30,965 --> 00:44:32,605
c'est pour ça qu'il est venu nous voir.
that's why he came to us.

904
00:44:32,685 --> 00:44:35,605
Ce que tu lui as dit, c'est ton affaire. Moi, je trouve ça long.
What you told him is your business.
For me, it's long.

905
00:44:36,445 --> 00:44:38,725
C'est long, c'est sombre, c'est…
It's long, it's dark, it's…

906
00:44:39,245 --> 00:44:42,445
Sanglant. C'est bien.
Bloody. It's good.

907
00:44:43,125 --> 00:44:44,885
C'est bien. Cet agneau est délicieux.
It's good. This lamb is wonderful.

908
00:44:45,525 --> 00:44:47,965
-Merci. -Qu'est-ce que vous mettez dans la sauce ?
-Thank you.
-What do you put in the sauce?

909
00:44:48,045 --> 00:44:51,045
-Pardon, je me permets. -Non, non… Je vous en prie.
-Sorry, I'm being overly familiar.
-No, no… Please.

910
00:44:52,885 --> 00:44:54,005
C'est un secret.
It's a secret.

911
00:44:55,125 --> 00:44:57,125
-Vous aimez ? -Oui, c'est excellent.
-Do you like it?
-Yes, delicious.

912
00:44:57,205 --> 00:44:59,245
Mais la violence est au cœur du projet.
But the violence is central
to the project.

913
00:44:59,325 --> 00:45:01,925
Je veux dire… C'est tout l'objet du film.
I mean…
It's the whole purpose of the movie.

914
00:45:02,005 --> 00:45:03,965
Xavier était catégorique là-dessus.
Xavier was adamant about that.

915
00:45:04,045 --> 00:45:05,205
Je pensais que « trop sanglant »
I thought "too bloody"

916
00:45:05,285 --> 00:45:07,565
n'existait plus depuis Game of Thrones. Non ?
was no longer a thing
since Game of Thrones. Right?

917
00:45:08,045 --> 00:45:09,325
Claire, s'il te plaît.
Claire, please.

918
00:45:16,925 --> 00:45:20,125
Oui. Eh bien, moi aussi j'ai lu le scénario, en fait.
Yes. Well, actually,
I too have read the script.

919
00:45:20,205 --> 00:45:21,205
Et j'ai quelques remarques.
And I have some notes.

920
00:45:21,965 --> 00:45:23,925
Je ne suis pas sûr que ce soit le bon moment.
I'm not sure this is a good time.

921
00:45:24,405 --> 00:45:25,245
Pourquoi pas ?
Why not?

922
00:45:26,005 --> 00:45:27,725
Je travaille avec vous maintenant, non ?
I work with you now, don't I?

923
00:45:28,445 --> 00:45:30,045
Je peux découper l'agneau et lire, aussi.
I can carve the lamb, and read too.

924
00:45:30,685 --> 00:45:32,565
-Noémie. -Bien sûr, pourquoi pas ?
-Noémie.
-Sure, why not?

925
00:45:33,285 --> 00:45:35,525
Je suis curieuse, si vous me le permettez ?
I'm curious, if you'll allow it?

926
00:45:36,885 --> 00:45:39,765
Je suis d'accord avec vous, Igor. C'est très violent.
I agree with you, Igor. It's very violent.

927
00:45:40,445 --> 00:45:42,085
-Oui, tout à fait. -Mais,
-Yes, it is.
-But,

928
00:45:42,605 --> 00:45:44,165
c'est l'intention du réalisateur
it's the intention of the director

929
00:45:44,245 --> 00:45:46,965
de montrer de façon réaliste et puissante
to show in a realistic and powerful way

930
00:45:47,405 --> 00:45:49,125
la violence même de l'époque.
the very violence of the era.

931
00:45:49,205 --> 00:45:50,205
Sa cruauté profonde.
Its very cruelty.

932
00:45:50,685 --> 00:45:54,365
Je crois que si vous le ressentez aussi fortement, c'est qu'il a réussi son pari.
I believe that if you feel so strongly
about it, it means he pulled it off.

933
00:45:55,645 --> 00:45:59,125
Quand on regarde les scènes de près, il n'y a pas tant de violence que ça.
When you take a close look at the scenes,
their isn't that much violence.

934
00:45:59,205 --> 00:46:00,845
-Enfin… -Ce n'est pas gratuit.
-Well…
-It's not gratuitous.

935
00:46:00,925 --> 00:46:04,085
C'est subtilement induit par le caractère des personnages.
It's subtly brought on
by the character of the people.

936
00:46:04,165 --> 00:46:06,685
Ils souffrent des contraintes qui leur sont imposées,
They suffer
from the restrictions imposed upon them,

937
00:46:06,765 --> 00:46:09,565
l'une après l'autre, et cette violence-là est extraordinaire.
one after another, and that sort
of violence is extraordinary.

938
00:46:09,645 --> 00:46:11,845
-Préci-- -Alors oui, ils prennent les armes.
-Preci--
-So, yes, they take up arms.

939
00:46:11,925 --> 00:46:13,885
Et que se passe-t-il ? On les traite de barbares.
And what happens?
They're called barbarians.

940
00:46:14,165 --> 00:46:17,405
La question que le film cherche à poser, c'est : qui sont les vrais barbares ?
The issue the film strives to address is:
who are the actual barbarians?

941
00:46:17,485 --> 00:46:18,885
Où est la vraie violence ?
Where is the actual violence?

942
00:46:19,885 --> 00:46:22,325
Dans la colère ouverte ? Ou dans les petites manœuvres sournoises ?
In outright anger?
Or in the dirty little tricks?

943
00:46:22,405 --> 00:46:25,725
Dans la malhonnêteté ordinaire ? Dans le mépris et l'abandon persistant
In casual dishonesty?
In disregard and in the unrelenting

944
00:46:25,805 --> 00:46:27,765
de l'idée du bien commun ?
abandonment of the idea
of the common good?

945
00:46:28,165 --> 00:46:30,885
Je pense à Brecht qui nous disait en son temps :
I am reminded of Brecht
who told us in his day:

946
00:46:30,965 --> 00:46:33,005
on parle souvent de la violence du fleuve,
we often talk about
the violence of the river,

947
00:46:33,085 --> 00:46:35,925
mais on ne parle jamais de la violence des berges qui le contiennent.
yet we never mention
the violence of the banks that contain it.

948
00:46:37,965 --> 00:46:40,725
Non ? Je veux dire… Pardon, mais…
Right? I mean… I'm sorry, but…

949
00:46:43,925 --> 00:46:46,925
Ça fait longtemps que je n'avais pas été aussi impressionné
It's been a long time
since I've been so impressed

950
00:46:47,005 --> 00:46:49,485
par quelqu'un avec qui je suis aussi profondément en désaccord.
by someone I so strongly disagree with.

951
00:46:55,325 --> 00:46:56,925
Tu es allé à l'audition de Macaigne ?
You went to the Macaigne audition?

952
00:46:57,005 --> 00:46:58,525
-Oui. Ça s'est bien passé. -Une bière ?
-Yes. It went pretty good.
-Beer?

953
00:46:58,605 --> 00:46:59,445
Non, merci.
No, thanks.

954
00:46:59,525 --> 00:47:00,885
Ouais. J'ai eu un rappel.
Yeah. I got a callback.

955
00:47:00,965 --> 00:47:01,805
C'est super.
That's great.

956
00:47:01,885 --> 00:47:03,125
-Tiens. -J'en suis content.
-Here.
-I'm happy about it.

957
00:47:03,205 --> 00:47:05,005
Mais je sais pas. Je veux dire…
But I don't know. I mean…

958
00:47:05,085 --> 00:47:07,445
Je crois que j'aimerais jouer dans un navet.
I think I'd like to play in a turkey.

959
00:47:07,525 --> 00:47:08,605
-Vraiment ? -Ouais.
-Really?
-Yeah.

960
00:47:09,165 --> 00:47:10,805
Mon agent me l'a déconseillé.
My agent advised me against it.

961
00:47:10,885 --> 00:47:13,125
C'est un peu bizarre, non ?
Well, it is a bit weird, isn't it?

962
00:47:13,205 --> 00:47:17,045
Non. Quand on y pense, les navets d'aujourd'hui sont les chefs-d'œuvre de demain.
No. When you think about it, today's
turkeys are tomorrow's masterpieces.

963
00:47:19,085 --> 00:47:19,925
Salut.
Hey.

964
00:47:20,485 --> 00:47:21,325
Salut.
Hey.

965
00:47:21,405 --> 00:47:22,645
-Bonjour. -Oh, salut.
-Hello.
-Oh, hi.

966
00:47:23,925 --> 00:47:26,845
Ravie de te voir, Sofia ne nous avait pas dit que tu venais.
It's great to see you,
Sofia didn't tell us you were coming.

967
00:47:26,925 --> 00:47:28,405
En fait, j'habite ici.
Actually, I live here.

968
00:47:28,485 --> 00:47:29,525
Ah, d'accord.
Oh, OK.

969
00:47:30,045 --> 00:47:32,125
-Je rentre du boulot. -Très bien.
-I'm coming from work.
-All right.

970
00:47:34,485 --> 00:47:36,285
Bon, j'ai du travail.
Right, I have work to do.

971
00:47:36,365 --> 00:47:37,205
Amusez-vous bien.
Have fun.

972
00:47:37,285 --> 00:47:38,125
-À bientôt. -Au revoir !
-See you.
-Bye!

973
00:47:38,205 --> 00:47:39,045
Au revoir.
Bye.

974
00:47:41,205 --> 00:47:42,405
Tu vis avec ton agent ?
You live with your agent?

975
00:47:42,485 --> 00:47:43,445
Ben, ouais.
Well, yeah.

976
00:47:43,925 --> 00:47:47,245
Non, attends. Règle n°1 : ton agent est ton agent.
No, hang on. Rule # 1 :
your agent is your agent.

977
00:47:47,325 --> 00:47:48,845
Pas ta copine.
Not your pal.

978
00:47:48,925 --> 00:47:50,965
Pas ton petit ami. Pas ta colocataire.
Not your boyfriend. Not your roommate.

979
00:47:51,925 --> 00:47:52,925
C'est ton agent.
She's your agent.

980
00:47:53,845 --> 00:47:56,125
Ouais, OK, mais c'est d'abord mon amie.
Yeah, OK, but she's my friend first.

981
00:47:56,205 --> 00:47:57,565
Mais alors c'est bizarre.
But then it's weird.

982
00:47:57,645 --> 00:48:00,285
Je ne peux pas parler de mon agent à cause du tien.
I can't talk about my agent now
because of your agent.

983
00:48:00,805 --> 00:48:02,125
On va prendre un verre ?
Should we go out for a drink?

984
00:48:02,205 --> 00:48:03,525
-Carrément. -Ouais. Alors…
-Definitely.
-Yeah. So…

985
00:48:03,605 --> 00:48:06,085
-Allez, Sofia, on va boire un verre. -Allons-y.
-Come on, Sofia, let's go have a drink.
-Let's.

986
00:48:06,165 --> 00:48:07,365
Allez, on y va.
Come on, let's go.

987
00:48:08,325 --> 00:48:09,925
Elle prend aussi 10 % sur le loyer ?
Does she also take 10% on the rent?

988
00:48:10,005 --> 00:48:11,325
Bon, ça suffit.
All right, cut it out.

989
00:48:28,365 --> 00:48:29,765
Allô, mo--
Hello, my--

990
00:48:29,845 --> 00:48:30,685
Agent.
Agent.

991
00:48:32,325 --> 00:48:33,205
« Mon agent. »
"My agent."

992
00:48:35,645 --> 00:48:36,845
Ça commence pareil.
It starts the same.

993
00:48:39,725 --> 00:48:41,325
-Entrez. -Excusez-moi.
-Come in.
-I'm sorry.

994
00:48:51,845 --> 00:48:52,685
Alors…
So…

995
00:48:54,765 --> 00:48:55,805
Il y a un service en chambre ?
Is there room service?

996
00:49:03,765 --> 00:49:05,085
Des nouvelles de Colette ?
Any news from Colette?

997
00:49:09,245 --> 00:49:11,365
J'ai merdé, je l'ai laissée partir.
I messed up, I let her leave.

998
00:49:12,285 --> 00:49:14,845
Il semble qu'on était destinés à passer cette soirée ensemble, en effet.
We were destined to spend
this evening together, indeed.

999
00:49:15,405 --> 00:49:16,525
On dirait bien.
It looks like it.

1000
00:49:21,605 --> 00:49:23,565
Elle m'a trompé mais je ne lui en veux pas parce que…
She cheated on me but I'm not mad because…

1001
00:49:24,845 --> 00:49:26,805
C'est moi qui l'ai trahie, d'une certaine façon.
I was the one who cheated her,
in some way.

1002
00:49:28,325 --> 00:49:29,165
C'est dingue.
It's crazy.

1003
00:49:30,725 --> 00:49:33,285
Je peux traverser Paris en courant pour une actrice au talon cassé,
I can run across Paris
for an actress with a broken heel,

1004
00:49:33,365 --> 00:49:35,565
mais quand ma femme me demande de rentrer
but when my wife asks me to be home

1005
00:49:35,645 --> 00:49:38,205
pour dîner avec elle et ma fille, je n'y arrive pas.
to have dinner with her and my daughter,
I can't do it.

1006
00:49:39,525 --> 00:49:42,085
Je ferais n'importe quoi pour mes acteurs, mais pas pour ma famille.
I'd do anything for my actors,
but not for my family.

1007
00:49:43,685 --> 00:49:45,685
Ça devrait être l'inverse.
It should be the other way around.

1008
00:49:47,085 --> 00:49:49,045
J'ai peut-être le cerveau mal câblé.
Maybe my brain is wired wrong.

1009
00:49:51,725 --> 00:49:52,765
Andréa.
Andréa.

1010
00:49:54,805 --> 00:49:55,685
José.
José.

1011
00:49:56,845 --> 00:49:57,725
Ta main.
Your hand.

1012
00:49:59,325 --> 00:50:02,125
Tu sais quoi ? Faisons un pacte.
You know what? Let's make a deal.

1013
00:50:02,205 --> 00:50:04,445
D'accord ? On va changer.
OK? We're going to change.

1014
00:50:04,525 --> 00:50:07,845
On va reprendre nos vies en main pour que ça n'arrive plus. OK ?
We're going to get our lives together
so that it doesn't happen again. OK?

1015
00:50:09,445 --> 00:50:10,725
Alors, je…
So, I…

1016
00:50:12,125 --> 00:50:16,085
Je promets d'arrêter de prendre des décisions à la légère. J'arrête, je réfléchis.
I promise to stop making rash decisions.
I'll stop, and think twice.

1017
00:50:16,165 --> 00:50:19,845
Sinon je vais me mettre en danger et tu ne seras pas là pour me sortir du pétrin.
Otherwise I'll put myself in danger
and you won't be there to bail me out.

1018
00:50:21,045 --> 00:50:21,885
Et toi ?
And you?

1019
00:50:24,245 --> 00:50:25,325
Je promets de--
I promise to--

1020
00:50:26,525 --> 00:50:27,525
Les profiteroles.
The profiteroles.

1021
00:50:28,125 --> 00:50:29,405
-Des profiteroles ? -Ouais.
-Profiteroles?
-Yeah.

1022
00:50:29,485 --> 00:50:31,285
C'était la dernière décision impulsive.
It was the last rash decision.

1023
00:50:31,365 --> 00:50:33,125
Quoi ? C'était une urgence.
What? It was an emergency.

1024
00:50:43,285 --> 00:50:44,405
Viens.
Come.

1025
00:50:48,085 --> 00:50:50,805
Je descends à la réception. J'ai un problème avec ma carte.
I'm going down to the lobby.
I have a problem with my card.

1026
00:50:52,085 --> 00:50:54,005
Mets ça sur la note de l'hôtel.
Just put it on the hotel bill.

1027
00:50:55,605 --> 00:50:57,405
Hein ? José ?
Huh? José?

1028
00:51:36,765 --> 00:51:39,445
Attends, attends. On peut trouver une solution.
Now, wait, hold on.
We can find a solution.

1029
00:51:39,525 --> 00:51:40,485
Oui, eh bien voilà !
Yes, well here!

1030
00:51:40,565 --> 00:51:42,045
Je viens de le trouver.
I just found it.

1031
00:51:42,125 --> 00:51:44,925
Dehors ! On n'engage pas un inconnu pour garder les bébés
You're out! You don't hire a stranger
to look after the babies

1032
00:51:45,005 --> 00:51:48,725
puis on laisse Capucine avec les enfants. Je ne le tolérerai pas. Allez, partez !
then leave Capucine with the children.
I won't stand for it. Now, go!

1033
00:51:51,525 --> 00:51:54,685
Hé, allez ! José Garcia n'est pas vraiment un inconnu.
Hey, come on!
José Garcia isn't really a stranger.

1034
00:51:55,325 --> 00:51:57,165
Et Capucine s'en est très bien sortie avec les enfants.
And Capucine did great with the kids.

1035
00:51:57,245 --> 00:51:58,485
Ils l'adorent. N'est-ce pas, Capu ?
They love her. Right, Capu?

1036
00:51:58,565 --> 00:52:00,285
-Oui. -Voilà.
-Yes.
-There.

1037
00:52:02,525 --> 00:52:03,685
Sale garce.
Stupid bitch.

1038
00:52:05,165 --> 00:52:06,925
C'est son nom, « Madame Sale-garce. »
That's her name, "Mrs. Stupid-bitch."

1039
00:52:09,165 --> 00:52:11,005
Bien, j'ai tout ce qu'il me faut.
Good, I have everything I need.

1040
00:52:11,085 --> 00:52:12,125
Merci.
Thank you.

1041
00:52:12,205 --> 00:52:13,965
-Hé. -Bonjour, Andréa.
-Hey.
-Hi, Andréa.

1042
00:52:15,525 --> 00:52:17,605
Tu inscris le gamin à des castings ?
Signing the kid up for auditions?

1043
00:52:17,685 --> 00:52:19,005
On nous a mis à la porte de la crèche.
They threw us out of daycare.

1044
00:52:20,885 --> 00:52:23,485
Allô ! Antoine, tu as reçu mes contrats ?
Hello! Antoine, did you get my contracts?

1045
00:52:23,565 --> 00:52:26,365
Tiens. Oh, attends, Sofia t'a laissé ça.
Here. Oh, wait, Sofia left this for you.

1046
00:52:26,845 --> 00:52:28,605
Elle m'a dit qu'elle en avait perdu 1 des 2
She told me that she lost 1 of the 2

1047
00:52:28,685 --> 00:52:31,485
et que ce serait bien si tu pouvais arranger ça avec Tiffany's.
and that it'd be nice
if you could sort it out with Tiffany's.

1048
00:52:31,565 --> 00:52:32,405
Quoi…
What…

1049
00:52:35,205 --> 00:52:36,205
Bonjour, Camille.
Hi, Camille.

1050
00:52:40,885 --> 00:52:41,845
Tu voulais me voir ?
You wanted to see me?

1051
00:52:42,405 --> 00:52:44,485
Oui. Hervé, ferme la porte, s'il te plaît ?
Yes. Hervé, shut the door, please?

1052
00:52:50,045 --> 00:52:51,525
Valérie, on vous écoute.
Valérie, we're listening.

1053
00:52:53,085 --> 00:52:54,845
-Bonjour, Hervé ! -Bonjour, Valérie.
-Hello, Hervé!
-Hi, Valérie.

1054
00:52:54,925 --> 00:52:55,765
Comment allez-vous ?
How are you?

1055
00:52:55,845 --> 00:52:56,685
Je vais bien.
I'm well.

1056
00:52:57,165 --> 00:52:58,605
J'ai une bonne nouvelle.
I have some good news.

1057
00:52:59,165 --> 00:53:00,765
Vous avez choisi mon Alex !
You picked my Alex!

1058
00:53:00,845 --> 00:53:03,445
Oh, non. Je suis désolée. Je n'ai toujours pas trouvé
Oh, no. I'm sorry. I still haven't found

1059
00:53:03,525 --> 00:53:07,125
Lucie, mais j'ai trouvé son frère.
Lucie, but I did find her brother.

1060
00:53:07,205 --> 00:53:08,885
Pourquoi vous me dites ça ?
Why are you telling me this?

1061
00:53:08,965 --> 00:53:11,725
Eh bien, parce que… Parce que c'est vous.
Well, because… Because it's you.

1062
00:53:11,805 --> 00:53:13,125
Vous seul pouvez jouer ce rôle.
Only you can play this part.

1063
00:53:13,685 --> 00:53:16,485
Vous étiez remarquable au casting.
I thought you were wonderful
at the audition.

1064
00:53:16,565 --> 00:53:18,285
Vraiment. Vous m'avez vraiment touchée.
Really. You really moved me.

1065
00:53:19,605 --> 00:53:21,165
On se retrouve pour en parler.
Let's get together, talk about it.

1066
00:53:21,245 --> 00:53:23,805
Élise, tu peux me rappeler quand vous avez fixé une date ?
Elise, can you call me back
when you've fixed up a date?

1067
00:53:23,885 --> 00:53:25,565
-Je m'en occupe. -Super, merci.
-I am on it.
-Great, thanks.

1068
00:53:25,645 --> 00:53:27,285
Hervé, à bientôt.
Hervé, see you soon.

1069
00:53:27,765 --> 00:53:29,885
-À bientôt, Valérie. -Je suis tellement heureuse.
-See you, Valérie.
-I'm so happy.

1070
00:53:33,485 --> 00:53:35,525
Je ne savais pas que tu voulais être acteur.
I didn't know you wanted to be actor.

1071
00:53:36,165 --> 00:53:37,205
Moi non plus.
Neither did I.

1072
00:53:37,725 --> 00:53:39,445
Beaucoup de gens ont commencé comme ça.
Lots of people started off that way.

1073
00:53:40,205 --> 00:53:42,245
Ils ont accompagné quelqu'un à un casting.
They went along with someone
to an audition.

1074
00:53:42,325 --> 00:53:44,125
Et finalement, ils ont décroché le rôle.
In the end, they got the part.

1075
00:53:44,885 --> 00:53:46,085
Tu crois que tu vas dire oui ?
You think you'll say yes?

1076
00:53:47,125 --> 00:53:48,565
Je sais que tu le feras.
I know you will.

1077
00:53:49,205 --> 00:53:51,045
Eh bien, je ne sais pas.
Well, look, I don't know.

1078
00:53:52,965 --> 00:53:56,525
C'est juste que je ne me vois pas l'annoncer à Gabriel. Je veux dire…
It's just that I can't see myself
telling Gabriel. I mean…

1079
00:53:57,245 --> 00:53:59,165
Personne ne t'y oblige.
Well, no one is making you.

1080
00:54:00,845 --> 00:54:01,885
De mon côté,
For my part,

1081
00:54:02,845 --> 00:54:04,885
Je suis très doué pour garder les secrets.
I'm very good at keeping secrets.

1082
00:54:08,885 --> 00:54:10,205
Vous voulez bien m'excuser ?
Will you excuse me?

1083
00:55:16,485 --> 00:55:18,485
Traduction des sous-titres par Carole Huguet
Subtitle translation by Carole Huguet
